-- הסכם קיבוצי (מסגרת) מיום 17.7.2023: the public-sector framework agreement
-- between the State and the public employers and the New General
-- Histadrut, for the time to 31.12.2027 (the cost of the wage agreements of
-- 1.1.2020–31.12.2027). Its introduction and whom it covers (chapters א–ג:
-- every employee of a signatory whose pay is computed by the collective
-- agreements of a scale the Histadrut represents, save annex א''s); a
-- one-time grant of up to 6,000 (ד: S = C·B·A); "תוספת שקלית 2023", 400 a
-- full position from 1.7.2023 and 500 from 1.10.2024 (ה); "תוספת אחוזית
-- 2024", 2% from 1.12.2024, 3.5% from 1.4.2025, 5% from 1.4.2026 and, by
-- default, 6% from 1.4.2027 (ו); the index-linked supplements brought
-- forward at the same rates (ז); the unique scales by annex ו' (ח); hourly
-- and daily workers (ט–י); the employees paid by the teaching employees'
-- salary, who have the framework's supplements less what the linkage to
-- that salary pays for 1.1.2020 on (יא); further negotiation over the last
-- 1% (יב); the special supplements raised (יג); the shorter working week —
-- 42 hours to 41 from 1.10.2023 (or 1.11.2023) and to 40 from 1.9.2024 (or
-- 1.8.2024) — the hour value, hourly workers, the reduction arrangements,
-- and the flexibility measures (יד); a day added to the Passover leave of
-- 5783 (טו); the agreement as one whole and the earlier agreements (טז–יז);
-- §19 of the 2016 framework amended for the payments of 2020–2023 (יח);
-- budgetary pensioners, S = Y + Z (יט); disputes cancelled, exhaustion of
-- claims, industrial peace, the follow-up committee and the arbitration
-- institution (כ–כד). Annexed: the scales it does not reach (א'), the
-- accession letters and the employers that cannot sign the first (ב'1–ב'3),
-- the employees whose shekel supplement stays 400 (ה'), the unique scales'
-- tables (ו'), examples of §70(ג) (ז'), the pensioners' scales and
-- coefficients (ח1'–ח4') and the disputes that stay open (ט).
--
-- The corpus publishes chapters ה and ו as one block each; §§24, 26, 35 and
-- 50 name their sub-chapters "(ה1)", "(ה2)", "ו(1)" and "ו'3", which the
-- corpus does not print. Each is read off the sections that name it: (ה1)
-- §§16–24 (paid from July 2023), (ה2) §§25–26 (paid from October 2024),
-- ו(1) §§27–35 (paid from December 2024), ו(3) §38 (the default of the last
-- 1%). Chapter יד's sub-chapters יד(1) (§§62–75) and יד(2) (§§76–79) are
-- printed.
--
-- It covers no teacher of the teachers' union: the Histadrut does not
-- represent the teaching scale. Chapter יא reaches the employees the
-- Histadrut represents whose pay follows the teaching employees' salary.
-- The Ofek Hadash wage agreement of 19.10.2022 is held against it month by
-- month in l4/tests/2022-10-19_ofek-hadash_wage-agreement-tests.l4. It
-- speaks to no pay item of l4/lib/vocabulary.l4 and is in no root.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT `2016-04-18_framework-agreement_public-sector`

§ `הסכם קיבוצי (מסגרת) — המגזר הציבורי (17.7.2023)`

DECLARE `2023 framework action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the 2023 grant in the August 2023 salary`
    `pay the 2023 grant in the January 2024 salary`
    `pay the 2023 grant in the last salary`
    `deduct the 2023 grant's advance in the salary that pays the grant`
    `pay the 2023 shekel supplement from the July 2023 salary`
    `pay the 2023 shekel supplement's July differences with the August salary`
    `pay the 2023 shekel supplement's rise from the October 2024 salary`
    `pay the 2023 shekel supplement's October differences with the November salary`
    `pay the 2024 percentage supplement from the December 2024 salary`
    `pay the 2024 percentage supplement's December differences with the January salary`
    `pay the 2024 percentage supplement's rise from the April salary`
    `pay the 2024 percentage supplement's April differences with the May salary`
    `pay the 2023 hourly shekel supplement from the July 2023 salary`
    `pay the 2023 hourly shekel supplement's rise from the October 2024 salary`
    `pay the 2023 daily shekel supplement from the July 2023 salary`
    `pay the 2023 daily shekel supplement's rise from the October 2024 salary`
    `raise an error in the list of employees paid by the teachers' salary`
    `negotiate another division of the last 1% of the 2023 framework`
    `transfer the salary data the Histadrut asks for under the 2023 framework`
    `examine a request to process salary data under the 2023 framework favourably`
    `declare a dispute for want of agreement on allocating the last 1%`
    `negotiate the 2024 percentage supplement's pulses to narrow the minimum-wage top-up`
    `go on discussing the structure of employment under the 2023 framework`
    `sign a follow-up decision on the firefighters' 2023 shekel supplement within 7 days`
    `negotiate an equivalent arrangement for the firefighters' 24-hour shifts`
    `sign a follow-up decision on the defence plants' shorter week within a week`
    `shorten the working week`
    `report a change in how the week is shortened to the wages commissioner and the Histadrut`
    `change how the week is shortened`
    `tell a part-time employee the updated position share`
    `pay a reduced-time hour worked as an overtime hour`
    `give information for the study of the shorter week`
    `cooperate with changes to role definitions`
    `declare a dispute over changes to role definitions`
    `move an employee whose role has become redundant`
    `create a substitute post close to a redundancy`
    `do the training a move requires`
    `bring a technological change to the Histadrut's knowledge`
    `declare a dispute or take measures that delay a new technology`
    `declare a dispute over a technological change`
    `choose between the 2023 flexibility measures and the employer's own`
    `notify the alternative leave day 14 days ahead`
    `notify that the Passover leave cannot be lengthened`
    `circulate the bill amending the Pensions Law under the 2023 framework`
    `support the bill amending the Pensions Law under the 2023 framework`
    `demand a further rise of the determining salary for the 2023 frame`
    `give another benefit for the 2023 pensioners' rise`
    `strike or harm the work over the productivity chapter to 31.12.2027`
    `strike or harm the work over a demand that costs the public employers`
    `negotiate further on pay for the period to 31.12.2027`
    `decide disputes over the 2023 framework agreement`
    `update the list of arbitrators within 90 days`
    `draw up a list of mediators within 90 days`

-- akn:preamble The agreement's frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:preamble/p1 The document's title; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p3 "Between"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p4 The State, by the wages commissioner or the Civil Service Commissioner, and for the defence plants the bodies authorised to sign for them; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p5 The Centre of Local Government, for every local authority save the three large cities; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p6 The three large cities and who represents them; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p7 The Centre of Regional Councils; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p8 The Union of Religious Councils; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p9 The National Insurance Institute; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p10 The Employment Service; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p11 The Hebrew University; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p12 Bar-Ilan University; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p13 Ben-Gurion University of the Negev; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p14 The University of Haifa; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p15 Tel Aviv University; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p16 The Technion; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p17 The Weizmann Institute; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p18 Clalit Health Services; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p19 The Hadassah Medical Organisation; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p20 The employers' short name; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p21 "On the one side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p22 "And"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p23 The Histadrut and who represents it; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p24 The Histadrut's short name; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p25 "On the other side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p26 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p28 A recital: the parties see importance in narrowing the public sector's pay gaps and raising its productivity; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p29 A recital: stability and certainty in labour relations and the budget, in view of the economic challenges; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p31 A recital: the importance of a shorter working week, excellence, flexibility and a work–home balance; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p32 A recital: the parties reached agreements on the shorter week and further productivity measures, which the agreement sets out; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p33 A recital: they anchor the agreements in this collective agreement; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p34 The words of agreement that introduce the clauses; no rule.

-- What the framework names and the corpus does not give it the words of,
-- stated once (MMS-538). The sub-chapter headings §§24, 26, 35 and 50 name
-- are not printed (read off the sections, as the head of this file says).
`the sub-chapter headings of the 2023 framework` MEANS
    `the text is missing` "כותרות פרקי המשנה (ה1), (ה2), ו(1), ו(2) ו־ו(3), שסעיפים 24, 26, 35 ו־50 מפנים אליהן"

-- The instruments it rests on that the corpus holds and this repository has
-- not encoded, and those the corpus does not hold.
`what the 2023 framework cites that is not encoded` MEANS
    LIST `not yet encoded` "ההסכם הקיבוצי מיום 16.9.2020 (\"עובד בהסדר\", סעיף 12(א)(2))",
         `not yet encoded` "ההסכם הקיבוצי בעניין טכנולוגיות מיום 10.1.2018 (סעיף 78(ד))"

`what the 2023 framework cites outside the corpus` MEANS
    LIST `outside the corpus` "ההסכם הקיבוצי בעניין שכר הסטודנטים שנחתם במקביל (סעיפים 42 ו־69(א))",
         `outside the corpus` "המסמך השמור בין הצדדים ובו שמות העובדים לפי סעיף 47(ג)",
         `outside the corpus` "ההסכם לפתרון בעיות שנחתם במקביל (סעיפים 100 ו־104(ז))",
         `outside the corpus` "חוזרי הממונה על השכר 2023-1-12 ו־2023-1-13 (סעיפים 15 ו־80)"

-- ¶2: the day of signing.
@ref akn:preamble/p2
`the 2023 framework agreement was signed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 17 7 2023

-- ¶27: the parties negotiated the cost of the wage agreements for the
-- employers' employees for 1.1.2020–31.12.2027, and for that time.
@ref akn:preamble/p27
`the 2023 framework's cost period opens on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020

-- ¶30: a uniform shekel supplement for every employee of every employer,
-- in every scale and grade, beside a uniform percentage supplement — which
-- chapters ה and ו set out.
@ref akn:preamble/p30
`the 2023 framework gives a uniform shekel and a uniform percentage supplement` MEANS TRUE

§§ `א מבוא וכללי (1–5)`

-- akn:chp_1 The heading of chapter א.

-- §1: the preamble and the annexes are part of the agreement. §2: its
-- headings are for convenience and do not bear on its reading — the
-- agreement itself answering what convention precedence.heading answers
-- where a text is silent. §3: an enactment is as amended from time to
-- time, or the one that replaces it. §4: naming an arrangement, procedure,
-- circular, letter, the Takshir or another administrative instruction
-- changes neither its standing nor whom it reaches. §5: the agreement
-- approves no deviation in pay under §29 of the Budget Foundations Law.
@ref akn:art_1
`the 2023 framework's preamble and annexes are part of it` MEANS TRUE

@ref akn:art_2
`the 2023 framework's headings bear on its reading` MEANS FALSE

@ref akn:art_3
`an enactment the 2023 framework names is read as amended from time to time` MEANS TRUE

@ref akn:art_4
`naming an administrative instruction in the 2023 framework changes its standing or reach` MEANS FALSE

@ref akn:art_5
`the 2023 framework approves a pay deviation under §29 of the Budget Foundations Law` MEANS FALSE

§§ `ב תקופת ההסכם (6)`

-- akn:chp_2 The heading of chapter ב.
-- akn:art_6/p2 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.

-- §6: the agreement is for the time to 31.12.2027 ("תקופת ההסכם"), the day
-- in (convention dates.end).
@ref akn:art_6
`the 2023 framework agreement's period ends on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2027

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the 2023 framework agreement's period` d IF
    d `is on or before` `the 2023 framework agreement's period ends on`

#ASSERT `in the 2023 framework agreement's period` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2027)
#ASSERT NOT `in the 2023 framework agreement's period` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2028)

§§ `ג תחולת ההסכם (7–9)`

-- akn:chp_3 The heading of chapter ג.

-- §7: the agreement covers every employee of an employer that signed it
-- whose pay is computed by the collective agreements of a scale the
-- Histadrut represents, save the scales annex א' lists ("עובד"), as the
-- agreement sets out. §9: and an employee of another employer, not a
-- signatory, that signs the accession letter of annex ב'1 on its terms —
-- save an employer annex ב'2 lists, for its employees that annex lists; ¶2:
-- for those, the provisions of annex ב'3 apply, if the employer signs it.
@desc An employee, as far as the framework agreement of 17.7.2023 asks.
DECLARE `2023 framework employee` HAS
    `employed by an employer that signed the 2023 framework` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed by an employer that signed annex ב'1 of 2023` IS A BOOLEAN
    `listed in annex ב'2 of 2023 with his employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `his employer signed annex ב'3 of 2023` IS A BOOLEAN
    `represented by the Histadrut under the 2023 framework` IS A BOOLEAN @desc his pay is computed by the collective agreements of a scale the New General Histadrut represents
    `his scale under the 2023 framework` IS A STRING @desc the scale's name, as annex א' or ח1' prints it
    `his pay is linked to a judicial officer's under the 2023 framework` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:art_7 akn:art_9
GIVEN e IS A `2023 framework employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2023 framework agreement covers` e IF
        e's `represented by the Histadrut under the 2023 framework`
    AND NOT `in a scale annex א' of 2023 keeps out` e
    AND (   e's `employed by an employer that signed the 2023 framework`
         OR (    e's `employed by an employer that signed annex ב'1 of 2023`
             AND NOT e's `listed in annex ב'2 of 2023 with his employer`))

-- §9 ¶2: an employee annex ב'2 lists with his employer is reached only by
-- what annex ב'3 joins, chapter יד and §§98 and 102, if his employer signs it.
@ref akn:art_9/p2
GIVEN e IS A `2023 framework employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `annex ב'3 of 2023 reaches` e IF
        e's `represented by the Histadrut under the 2023 framework`
    AND e's `listed in annex ב'2 of 2023 with his employer`
    AND e's `his employer signed annex ב'3 of 2023`

-- ¶3: joining with adjustments or changes other than the attached letter
-- needs the approval of the chairman of the trade-union division, and for a
-- "funded" or "supported" body (Budget Foundations Law) the wages
-- commissioner's too.
@ref akn:art_9/p3
GIVEN `the chairman approved` IS A BOOLEAN, `a funded or supported body` IS A BOOLEAN, `the wages commissioner approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 2023 accession with changes holds` `the chairman approved` `a funded or supported body` `the wages commissioner approved` IF
    `the chairman approved` AND ((NOT `a funded or supported body`) OR `the wages commissioner approved`)

#ASSERT `a 2023 accession with changes holds` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `a 2023 accession with changes holds` TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- §8: the payments under the agreement, and under the agreements of
-- chapter יב, go to an employee employed in the months they are paid; ¶2:
-- chapter יט (budgetary pensioners) reaches whom it says. §10 takes the
-- grant out of §8.
@ref akn:art_8 akn:art_8/p2
GIVEN `employed in the month of the payment` IS A BOOLEAN, `the payment is the 2023 grant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 2023 framework payment goes to the employee` `employed in the month of the payment` `the payment is the 2023 grant` IF
    `the payment is the 2023 grant` OR `employed in the month of the payment`

§§ `ד מענק חד פעמי (10–15)`

-- akn:chp_4 The heading of chapter ד: a one-time grant, 6,000 in all.
-- akn:art_11 The heading of §11: "in this chapter".
-- akn:art_11__hc_2__para_a/p2 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.
-- akn:art_12/p5 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.
-- akn:art_12/p15 The heading of the clarifications on computing B and C; no rule.
-- akn:art_12__para_b/p2 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.
-- akn:art_13__para_c/p2 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.
-- akn:art_14 The heading of §14: when the grant is paid.

-- Time in salary months: month m of year y is y·12 + m, and a salary "for"
-- a month is that month's (convention dates.salary-month).
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2023 framework's month` y m IS
    y TIMES 12 PLUS m

-- The absences §§11 and 12 count or leave out of a run of employment.
DECLARE `2023 grant absence` IS ONE OF
    `unpaid leave under the 2023 framework`
    `leave treated as unpaid under the 2023 framework`
    `reserve duty under the 2023 framework`
    `birth and parenthood leave under the 2023 framework`
    `sick leave of Takshir 33.210 under the 2023 framework`
    `paid absence the employer approved under the 2023 framework`

-- §11 (ג) and (ד): in counting the run, unpaid leave or leave treated as
-- unpaid is not counted (1); reserve duty, birth and parenthood leave under
-- the Women's Employment Law and sick leave of Takshir 33.210 — on full,
-- half or no pay — are (2); ¶2: an absence the employer approved and paid
-- (rest leave, paid study) does not break it.
@ref akn:art_11__hc_2__para_c akn:art_11__hc_2__para_c__subpara_1 akn:art_11__hc_2__para_c__subpara_2 akn:art_11__hc_2/p2 akn:art_11__hc_3__para_d akn:art_11__hc_3__para_d__subpara_1 akn:art_11__hc_3__para_d__subpara_2 akn:art_11__hc_3/p2
GIVEN a IS A `2023 grant absence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 2023 grant absence keeps the run` a IF
    NOT (   a EQUALS `unpaid leave under the 2023 framework`
         OR a EQUALS `leave treated as unpaid under the 2023 framework`)

#ASSERT `a 2023 grant absence keeps the run` `reserve duty under the 2023 framework`
#ASSERT `a 2023 grant absence keeps the run` `paid absence the employer approved under the 2023 framework`
#ASSERT NOT `a 2023 grant absence keeps the run` `unpaid leave under the 2023 framework`

-- §11: the employee "for the grant" is one in the qualifying period or in
-- the completion period.
@desc An employee as far as chapter ד asks.
DECLARE `2023 grant employee` HAS
    `employed on 1.3.2023 in a qualifying scale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc by one of the employers, his pay computed by the agreements of a scale the Histadrut represents and annex א' does not list ("הדירוגים המזכים")
    `employed by the same employer on 1.6.2022` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a run in qualifying scales to 28.2.2023, by §11(ג)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the run unbroken by §11(ג)'s count, every day of it in a qualifying scale
    `began with the employer before 1.6.2022 in a qualifying scale` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a scale not qualifying during the qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on unpaid leave or so absent during the qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `full months of salary in a run in qualifying scales, 1.10.2021–31.12.2023` IS A NUMBER @desc the longest run, counted by §11(ד)

-- "עובד בתקופת האכשרה": (א) employed on 1.3.2023 in a qualifying scale; (ב)
-- employed by the same employer on 1.6.2022 and without a break to
-- 28.2.2023, every day of it in a qualifying scale ("תקופת האכשרה"), the
-- run counted by (ג).
@ref akn:art_11__hc_2 akn:art_11__hc_2__para_a akn:art_11__hc_2__para_b
GIVEN e IS A `2023 grant employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 2023 qualifying-period employee` e IF
        e's `employed on 1.3.2023 in a qualifying scale`
    AND e's `employed by the same employer on 1.6.2022`
    AND e's `a run in qualifying scales to 28.2.2023, by §11(ג)`

`the 2023 qualifying period opens on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2022
`the 2023 qualifying period ends on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2023
`the 2023 completion period opens on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2021
`the 2023 completion period ends on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2023
`the full months of salary the completion period asks` MEANS 9

-- "עובד בתקופת ההשלמה": (א) employed on 1.3.2023 in a qualifying scale; (ב)
-- began with that employer before 1.6.2022 in a qualifying scale; (ג) and
-- either (1) was in the qualifying period, wholly or in part, in a scale
-- that does not qualify, or (2) was then on unpaid leave or absent as if on
-- unpaid leave — and in 1.10.2021–31.12.2023 ("תקופת ההשלמה") was or will
-- be entitled to salary for at least 9 full months in a run in qualifying
-- scales, the run counted by (ד).
@ref akn:art_11__hc_3 akn:art_11__hc_3__para_a akn:art_11__hc_3__para_b akn:art_11__hc_3__para_c akn:art_11__hc_3__para_c__subpara_1 akn:art_11__hc_3__para_c__subpara_2
GIVEN e IS A `2023 grant employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 2023 completion-period employee` e IF
        e's `employed on 1.3.2023 in a qualifying scale`
    AND e's `began with the employer before 1.6.2022 in a qualifying scale`
    AND (e's `in a scale not qualifying during the qualifying period` OR e's `on unpaid leave or so absent during the qualifying period`)
    AND e's `full months of salary in a run in qualifying scales, 1.10.2021–31.12.2023` AT LEAST `the full months of salary the completion period asks`

@ref akn:art_11__hc_1
GIVEN e IS A `2023 grant employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an employee for the 2023 grant` e IF
    `a 2023 qualifying-period employee` e OR `a 2023 completion-period employee` e

-- §10: such an employee has a one-time grant by this chapter; §8 does not
-- apply to it (the grant does not ask for employment in the month it is
-- paid).
@ref akn:art_10
`§8 applies to the 2023 grant` MEANS FALSE

-- One on unpaid leave in the summer of 2022 who came back to a qualifying
-- scale and was paid for nine full months in a run.
`a returner of 2023` MEANS
    `2023 grant employee` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE 9

#ASSERT NOT `a 2023 qualifying-period employee` `a returner of 2023`
#ASSERT `a 2023 completion-period employee` `a returner of 2023`
#ASSERT `an employee for the 2023 grant` `a returner of 2023`

-- §12: S = C · B · A, in shekels. A is 6,000; B the months the employee was
-- employed in the calculation period, 1.10.2020–31.3.2023, divided by 30
-- ("חודשי חישוב העסקה"); C the mean position share in those months
-- ("חודשי חישוב חלקיות המשרה"). ¶14: S is rounded to the nearest whole
-- shekel, a half up (convention rounding.half).
@ref akn:art_12 akn:art_12/p2 akn:art_12/p3 akn:art_12/p4 akn:art_12/p6 akn:art_12/p8 akn:art_12/p14
`A of the 2023 grant` MEANS 6000
`the months of the 2023 grant's calculation period` MEANS 30
`the 2023 grant's calculation period opens on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2020
`the 2023 grant's calculation period ends on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2023

GIVEN `months employed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `B of the 2023 grant` `months employed` IS
    `months employed` DIVIDED BY `the months of the 2023 grant's calculation period`

GIVEN `months employed` IS A NUMBER, C IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2023 grant` `months employed` C IS
    `to the nearest whole` (C TIMES `B of the 2023 grant` `months employed` TIMES `A of the 2023 grant`)

-- The calculation period runs thirty months.
#ASSERT `the 2023 framework's month` 2023 3 MINUS `the 2023 framework's month` 2020 10 PLUS 1 EQUALS `the months of the 2023 grant's calculation period`

-- ¶7: a month employed in part counts in proportion — the days employed
-- that month over the days of employment in it.
@ref akn:art_12/p7
GIVEN `days employed` IS A NUMBER, `days of employment in the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a part month of the 2023 grant` `days employed` `days of employment in the month` IS
    `days employed` DIVIDED BY `days of employment in the month`

#ASSERT `a part month of the 2023 grant` 11 22 EQUALS 0.5

-- ¶9–¶13: an employee of the State, in a qualifying scale for 24 of the 30
-- months, at 75%: A = 6,000, B = 24/30, C = 3/4, S = 3,600.
@ref akn:art_12/p9 akn:art_12/p10 akn:art_12/p11 akn:art_12/p12 akn:art_12/p13
#ASSERT `B of the 2023 grant` 24 EQUALS 24 DIVIDED BY 30
#ASSERT `the 2023 grant` 24 (3 DIVIDED BY 4) EQUALS 3600

-- (א): in computing B and C, (1) unpaid leave or leave treated as unpaid is
-- left out; (2) reserve duty, birth and parenthood leave, sick leave of
-- Takshir 33.210, and time as an "עובד בהסדר" under the agreement of
-- 16.9.2020 are counted; ¶2: such an employee's share of a position for C
-- is computed as that agreement computes it for its special payment (a
-- named input: the agreement of 16.9.2020 is the corpus's and not encoded
-- here); ¶3: an absence the employer approved and paid counts for B and C.
@ref akn:art_12__para_a akn:art_12__para_a__subpara_1 akn:art_12__para_a__subpara_2 akn:art_12__para_a__subpara_2/p3
GIVEN a IS A `2023 grant absence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 2023 grant absence counts for B and C` a IF
    `a 2023 grant absence keeps the run` a

`time as an employee in the arrangement of 16.9.2020 counts for B and C` MEANS TRUE

@ref akn:art_12__para_a__subpara_2/p2
GIVEN `the share the agreement of 16.9.2020 computes for its special payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a furloughed employee's share for C of 2023` `the share the agreement of 16.9.2020 computes for its special payment` IS
    `the share the agreement of 16.9.2020 computes for its special payment`

-- (ב): notwithstanding (א), for the months B counts, and for that alone, in
-- view of the corona crisis, by exception and without precedent: for
-- 1.10.2020–30.6.2021, and for it alone, unpaid leave and leave treated as
-- unpaid count too — for a scale whose employees were sent on unpaid leave
-- for the corona period.
@ref akn:art_12__para_b
`the corona window of the 2023 grant ends on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2021

GIVEN a IS A `2023 grant absence`, d IS A DATE, `a scale sent on unpaid leave for the corona` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 2023 grant absence counts for B on` a d `a scale sent on unpaid leave for the corona` IF
        `a 2023 grant absence counts for B and C` a
    OR (    `a scale sent on unpaid leave for the corona`
        AND d `is on or after` `the 2023 grant's calculation period opens on`
        AND d `is on or before` `the corona window of the 2023 grant ends on`)

#ASSERT `a 2023 grant absence counts for B on` `unpaid leave under the 2023 framework` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2021) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a 2023 grant absence counts for B on` `unpaid leave under the 2023 framework` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2021) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a 2023 grant absence counts for B on` `unpaid leave under the 2023 framework` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2021) FALSE

-- The illustration (¶3–¶10): employed from 15.1.2021, in a scale sent on
-- unpaid leave, on unpaid leave 1.3.2021–1.5.2021 and 1.8.21–1.1.2022, at a
-- full position whenever employed and not on leave. For 15.1.2021–30.6.21
-- the 5.5 months all count, the first leave being in the corona window;
-- for 1.7.2021–31.3.2023, 16 of the 21 months; B = 21.5/30, which the text
-- prints 0.716 — truncated, not rounded (0.71666…); and C = 1, counting
-- only the months employed and not on leave. The example illustrates and S
-- is rounded only at the end (¶14), so nothing turns on the third decimal.
@ref akn:art_12__para_b/p3 akn:art_12__para_b/p4 akn:art_12__para_b__subpara_1 akn:art_12__para_b__subpara_2 akn:art_12__para_b__subpara_3 akn:art_12__para_b__subpara_4 akn:art_12__para_b/p5 akn:art_12__para_b/p6 akn:art_12__para_b/p7 akn:art_12__para_b/p8 akn:art_12__para_b/p9 akn:art_12__para_b/p10
`the illustration's months to 30.6.2021` MEANS 5.5
`the illustration's months from 1.7.2021` MEANS
    (`the 2023 framework's month` 2023 3 MINUS `the 2023 framework's month` 2021 7 PLUS 1)
    MINUS (`the 2023 framework's month` 2021 12 MINUS `the 2023 framework's month` 2021 8 PLUS 1)

#ASSERT `the illustration's months from 1.7.2021` EQUALS 16
#ASSERT `B of the 2023 grant` (`the illustration's months to 30.6.2021` PLUS `the illustration's months from 1.7.2021`) EQUALS 21.5 DIVIDED BY 30
#ASSERT TRUNC (`B of the 2023 grant` 21.5) 3 EQUALS 0.716
#ASSERT `the 2023 grant` 21.5 1 EQUALS 4300

-- (ג): C for one paid by the hour or the day, by an auxiliary mean
-- position share over the months C counts: (1) by the hour (students, for
-- one), the mean monthly hours worked over 182; (2) by the day, the mean
-- monthly days worked over 20.83 at a five-day workplace or over 25 at a
-- six-day one.
@ref akn:art_12__para_c akn:art_12__para_c__subpara_1
GIVEN `mean monthly hours worked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `C of 2023 for one paid by the hour` `mean monthly hours worked` IS
    `mean monthly hours worked` DIVIDED BY 182

@ref akn:art_12__para_c__subpara_2
GIVEN `mean monthly days worked` IS A NUMBER, `a five-day workplace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `C of 2023 for one paid by the day` `mean monthly days worked` `a five-day workplace` IS
    IF `a five-day workplace`
    THEN `mean monthly days worked` DIVIDED BY 20.83
    ELSE `mean monthly days worked` DIVIDED BY 25

#ASSERT `C of 2023 for one paid by the hour` 91 EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `C of 2023 for one paid by the day` 12.5 FALSE EQUALS 0.5

-- §13: the grant is not salary for any purpose: it counts for no hour
-- value, overtime and its kin, percentage supplement, severance pay, unused
-- sick days, vacation redemption or budgetary pension's determining salary,
-- and no provident-fund contribution is made on it. ¶2, (א): naming a
-- component gives no right to it; (ב) it is not counted for topping up to
-- the minimum wage; (ג) it does not change the salary base by the tables of
-- the scale and grade on the eve of the signing.
DECLARE `what the 2023 framework's payments might count for` IS ONE OF
    `the hour value under the 2023 framework`
    `overtime, stand-by, call-outs, shifts and incentive pay under the 2023 framework`
    `percentage supplements under the 2023 framework`
    `severance pay under the 2023 framework`
    `unused sick days under the 2023 framework`
    `vacation redemption under the 2023 framework`
    `the determining salary of a budgetary pension under the 2023 framework`
    `provident and training-fund contributions under the 2023 framework`
    `topping up to the minimum wage under the 2023 framework`
    `the base of the supplements of the eve under the 2023 framework`

@ref akn:art_13 akn:art_13/p2 akn:art_13__para_a akn:art_13__para_b
GIVEN p IS A `what the 2023 framework's payments might count for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2023 grant counts for` p IF
    FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the 2023 grant counts for` `topping up to the minimum wage under the 2023 framework`

@ref akn:art_13__para_c
`the 2023 grant changes the salary base of the tables` MEANS FALSE

-- §14: when the grant is paid. (א) to a qualifying-period employee in the
-- salary for August 2023, at the latest September 2023's; (ב) to a
-- completion-period employee, (1) if he completed the run in the month
-- before that payment, with it, and (2) if later, in the salary for January
-- 2024, at the latest February 2024's; ¶: one whose employment ends before,
-- in the last salary paid him.
DECLARE `2023 grant payment` HAS
    `the salary month the grant is due in` IS A NUMBER
    `the last salary month it may be paid in` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_14__para_a akn:art_14__para_b akn:art_14__para_b__subpara_1 akn:art_14__para_b__subpara_2 akn:art_14/p1
GIVEN `a qualifying-period employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month he completed the run` IS A NUMBER
      `the last salary month he is employed in` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `2023 grant payment`
DECIDE `when the 2023 grant is paid` `a qualifying-period employee` `the month he completed the run` `the last salary month he is employed in` IS
    IF `the last salary month he is employed in` LESS THAN `the due month`
    THEN `2023 grant payment` `the last salary month he is employed in` `the last salary month he is employed in`
    ELSE `2023 grant payment` `the due month` (`the due month` PLUS 1)
    WHERE
        `the qualifying payment` MEANS `the 2023 framework's month` 2023 8
        `paid with the qualifying` MEANS
            `a qualifying-period employee` OR `the month he completed the run` AT MOST `the qualifying payment` MINUS 1
        `the due month` MEANS
            IF `paid with the qualifying` THEN `the qualifying payment` ELSE `the 2023 framework's month` 2024 1

#ASSERT `when the 2023 grant is paid` TRUE 0 (`the 2023 framework's month` 2030 1) EQUALS `2023 grant payment` (`the 2023 framework's month` 2023 8) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2023 9)
#ASSERT `when the 2023 grant is paid` FALSE (`the 2023 framework's month` 2023 10) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2030 1) EQUALS `2023 grant payment` (`the 2023 framework's month` 2024 1) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2024 2)
#ASSERT `when the 2023 grant is paid` FALSE (`the 2023 framework's month` 2023 7) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2030 1) EQUALS `2023 grant payment` (`the 2023 framework's month` 2023 8) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2023 9)
#ASSERT `when the 2023 grant is paid` FALSE (`the 2023 framework's month` 2023 10) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2023 11) EQUALS `2023 grant payment` (`the 2023 framework's month` 2023 11) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2023 11)

`paying the 2023 grant` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the 2023 grant in the August 2023 salary`
    LEST  (PARTY `the employer`
           MUST  `pay the 2023 grant in the last salary`)

-- §15: an advance paid under the wages commissioner's circular 2023-1-12
-- is deducted from the salary at the grant's payment.
@ref akn:art_15
GIVEN `the grant` IS A NUMBER, `the advance paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2023 grant less its advance` `the grant` `the advance paid` IS
    `the grant` MINUS `the advance paid`

`deducting the 2023 grant's advance` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `deduct the 2023 grant's advance in the salary that pays the grant`

§§ `ה תוספת שקלית אחידה (16–26)`

-- akn:chp_5 The heading of chapter ה: a uniform shekel supplement.
-- akn:art_19/p2 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.

-- Who chapters ה and ו set apart, each by an arrangement of its own.
DECLARE `2023 framework pay basis` IS ONE OF
    `paid monthly under the 2023 framework`
    `in a unique scale under the 2023 framework`
    `a student paid by the hour under the 2023 framework`
    `paid by the hour under the 2023 framework`
    `paid by the day under the 2023 framework`
    `a teaching assistant of notice 12/2023 under the 2023 framework`
    `a firefighter under the 2023 framework`
    `paid by the teaching employees' salary under the 2023 framework`

-- §16: from 1.7.2023 the employees, save §17's, have a new monthly shekel
-- supplement of 400 for a full position ("תוספת שקלית 2023"), the same sum
-- for every employee of every scale and grade; for those paid by the
-- teaching employees' salary, as chapter יא says. §17: not (א) the unique
-- scales (chapter ח); (ב) those paid by the hour, students among them
-- (chapter ט); (ג) those paid by the day (chapter י); (ד) those under the
-- employees' notice 12/2023 of 4.4.2023 on teaching assistants ("תומכות
-- חינוך"); (ה) the firefighters, for whom a follow-up decision is signed
-- within 7 days — each having another arrangement of the supplement.
@ref akn:art_16 akn:art_17 akn:art_17__para_a akn:art_17__para_b akn:art_17__para_c akn:art_17__para_d akn:art_17__para_e
GIVEN b IS A `2023 framework pay basis`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `chapter ה of 2023 reaches` b IF
        b EQUALS `paid monthly under the 2023 framework`
    OR  b EQUALS `paid by the teaching employees' salary under the 2023 framework`

`the 2023 shekel supplement starts on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2023
`the 2023 shekel supplement for a full position` MEANS 400

`signing the firefighters' 2023 follow-up decision` MEANS
    PARTY `the follow-up committee`
    MUST  `sign a follow-up decision on the firefighters' 2023 shekel supplement within 7 days`

-- §25: from 1.10.2024 the supplement grows by 100 to 500 for a full
-- position, its other rules unchanged — save for (א) the employees annex ה'
-- lists and (ב) those the parties agree by 1.9.2024 are not entitled, for
-- whom it stays 400. ¶2: for an employer under §29 of the Budget
-- Foundations Law, subject to it.
@ref akn:art_25 akn:art_25__para_a akn:art_25__para_b akn:art_25__para_b/p2
`the 2023 shekel supplement grows on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2024
`the 2023 shekel supplement's rise` MEANS 100
`the last day to agree who stays at 400` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2024

GIVEN d IS A DATE, `stays at 400` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2023 shekel supplement for a full position on` d `stays at 400` IS
    IF NOT d `is on or after` `the 2023 shekel supplement starts on`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF d `is on or after` `the 2023 shekel supplement grows on` AND NOT `stays at 400`
         THEN `the 2023 shekel supplement for a full position` PLUS `the 2023 shekel supplement's rise`
         ELSE `the 2023 shekel supplement for a full position`

#ASSERT `the 2023 shekel supplement for a full position on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2023) FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the 2023 shekel supplement for a full position on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2023) FALSE EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `the 2023 shekel supplement for a full position on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2024) FALSE EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `the 2023 shekel supplement for a full position on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2024) TRUE EQUALS 400

-- §18: a part-time employee has it in proportion to his position against
-- a full one (convention position.above-full).
@ref akn:art_18
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `stays at 400` IS A BOOLEAN, `position share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2023 shekel supplement on` d `stays at 400` `position share` IS
    (`the 2023 shekel supplement for a full position on` d `stays at 400`) `pro rata to a position of` `position share`

#ASSERT `the 2023 shekel supplement on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2024) FALSE 0.5 EQUALS 250

-- §19: it is not counted for topping up to the minimum wage. §20: it is
-- salary for every purpose — the hour value, overtime, stand-by, duty
-- rosters, shifts, call-outs and incentive pay, severance pay, pensions,
-- pension, training-fund and every other contribution usual on the combined
-- salary; naming a component gives no right to it. §23: the Government
-- says that by §8 of the Pensions Law it is counted in the determining
-- salary. §21: it is not in the base of any supplement existing on the eve
-- of the signing; future supplements follow their own rules.
@ref akn:art_19 akn:art_20 akn:art_21 akn:art_23
GIVEN p IS A `what the 2023 framework's payments might count for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2023 shekel supplement counts for` p IF
    NOT (   p EQUALS `topping up to the minimum wage under the 2023 framework`
         OR p EQUALS `the base of the supplements of the eve under the 2023 framework`
         OR p EQUALS `percentage supplements under the 2023 framework`
         OR p EQUALS `unused sick days under the 2023 framework`
         OR p EQUALS `vacation redemption under the 2023 framework`)

#ASSERT `the 2023 shekel supplement counts for` `the determining salary of a budgetary pension under the 2023 framework`
#ASSERT NOT `the 2023 shekel supplement counts for` `topping up to the minimum wage under the 2023 framework`

-- §22: from the end of the agreement's period it is updated at the rates
-- of the cost-of-living supplements, on their payment days.
@ref akn:art_22
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the cost-of-living rates paid since the period's end` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the supplement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2023 shekel supplement updated after the period` d `the cost-of-living rates paid since the period's end` `the supplement` IS
    IF d `is on or before` `the 2023 framework agreement's period ends on`
    THEN `the supplement`
    ELSE foldl (GIVEN acc, r YIELD acc `increased by` r) `the supplement` `the cost-of-living rates paid since the period's end`

#ASSERT `the 2023 shekel supplement updated after the period` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2028) (LIST (2%)) 500 EQUALS 510

-- §24: the payments of sub-chapter (ה1) — §§16–23 — are paid from the
-- salary for July 2023, at the latest from August's, and if from August's,
-- with July's differences (convention dates.salary-month). §26: those of
-- (ה2) — §25 — from the salary for October 2024, at the latest from
-- November's, with October's differences.
@ref akn:art_24
`paying the 2023 shekel supplement` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the 2023 shekel supplement from the July 2023 salary`
    LEST  (PARTY `the employer`
           MUST  `pay the 2023 shekel supplement's July differences with the August salary`)

@ref akn:art_26
`paying the 2023 shekel supplement's rise` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the 2023 shekel supplement's rise from the October 2024 salary`
    LEST  (PARTY `the employer`
           MUST  `pay the 2023 shekel supplement's October differences with the November salary`)

-- The salary a pulse is first paid with, and the month whose differences
-- it carries if paid a month late: the month the pulse starts in.
DECLARE `2023 pulse payment` HAS
    `the pulse's first salary month` IS A NUMBER
    `the latest salary month to start paying it` IS A NUMBER
    `the month whose differences a late start pays` IS A NUMBER

`the payments of (ה1)` MEANS `2023 pulse payment` (`the 2023 framework's month` 2023 7) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2023 8) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2023 7)
`the payments of (ה2)` MEANS `2023 pulse payment` (`the 2023 framework's month` 2024 10) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2024 11) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2024 10)

GIVEN p IS A `2023 pulse payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a late start pays the pulse's own first month` p IF
    p's `the month whose differences a late start pays` EQUALS p's `the pulse's first salary month`

#ASSERT `a late start pays the pulse's own first month` `the payments of (ה1)`
#ASSERT `a late start pays the pulse's own first month` `the payments of (ה2)`

§§ `ו תוספת אחוזית 2024 (27–38)`

-- akn:chp_6 The heading of chapter ו: the 2024 percentage supplement.
-- akn:art_27/p2 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.
-- akn:art_35/p2 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.

-- §27: from 1.12.2024 the employees, save §28's, have a new pay supplement
-- of 2% ("תוספת אחוזית 2024"), the same rate for every employee of every
-- scale and grade; for those paid by the teaching employees' salary, as
-- chapter יא says. §28: not (א) the unique scales (ח); (ב) the students (ט);
-- (ג) those under notice 12/2023 on teaching assistants. Those paid by the
-- hour or the day otherwise, and the firefighters, are not set apart here.
@ref akn:art_27 akn:art_28 akn:art_28__para_a akn:art_28__para_b akn:art_28__para_c
GIVEN b IS A `2023 framework pay basis`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `chapter ו of 2023 reaches` b IF
    NOT (   b EQUALS `in a unique scale under the 2023 framework`
         OR b EQUALS `a student paid by the hour under the 2023 framework`
         OR b EQUALS `a teaching assistant of notice 12/2023 under the 2023 framework`)

#ASSERT `chapter ו of 2023 reaches` `paid by the hour under the 2023 framework`
#ASSERT NOT `chapter ה of 2023 reaches` `paid by the hour under the 2023 framework`

-- §36: from 1.4.2025 the rate rises by 1.5% (by addition) from 2% to 3.5%;
-- §37: from 1.4.2026 by 1.5% to 5%; §38: from 1.4.2027 by 1% to 6% — save
-- that (¶2), for the employees §50 reaches, only if no collective agreement
-- allocating the cost as §50 says is signed by 31.1.2027, and in any case
-- with no double payment and no further negotiation over that cost. This is
-- the default sub-chapter ו'3 that §50 names.
@desc A step of the 2024 percentage supplement: its day and the rate it brings the supplement to.
DECLARE `2024 percentage step` HAS
    `the 2024 step's day` IS A DATE
    `the 2024 step's rate` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_36 akn:art_37 akn:art_38 akn:art_38/p2
`the steps of the 2024 percentage supplement` MEANS
    LIST `2024 percentage step` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2024) (2%),
         `2024 percentage step` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2025) (3.5%),
         `2024 percentage step` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2026) (5%),
         `2024 percentage step` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2027) (6%)

`the last day to agree another division of the last 1%` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 1 2027

-- The rate on a day; `the last 1% goes by default` is FALSE for an
-- employee §50 reaches whose agreement under §50 was signed by 31.1.2027.
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the last 1% goes by default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2024 percentage supplement rate on` d `the last 1% goes by default` IS
    foldl (GIVEN acc, s YIELD
               IF d `is on or after` (s's `the 2024 step's day`)
                  AND (`the last 1% goes by default` OR s's `the 2024 step's rate` LESS THAN 6%)
               THEN s's `the 2024 step's rate`
               ELSE acc)
          0 `the steps of the 2024 percentage supplement`

#ASSERT `the 2024 percentage supplement rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 11 2024) TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the 2024 percentage supplement rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2024) TRUE EQUALS 2%
#ASSERT `the 2024 percentage supplement rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2025) TRUE EQUALS 3.5%
#ASSERT `the 2024 percentage supplement rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2026) TRUE EQUALS 5%
#ASSERT `the 2024 percentage supplement rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2027) TRUE EQUALS 6%
#ASSERT `the 2024 percentage supplement rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2027) FALSE EQUALS 5%

-- Each step adds what its section says, by addition: 2%, then 1.5%, 1.5%
-- and 1%.
#ASSERT `the 2024 percentage supplement rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2025) TRUE MINUS `the 2024 percentage supplement rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2024) TRUE EQUALS 1.5%
#ASSERT `the 2024 percentage supplement rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2026) TRUE MINUS `the 2024 percentage supplement rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2025) TRUE EQUALS 1.5%
#ASSERT `the 2024 percentage supplement rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2027) TRUE MINUS `the 2024 percentage supplement rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2026) TRUE EQUALS 1%

`no double payment for the last 1%` MEANS TRUE

-- §29: the supplement's base is the combined salary, the seniority
-- supplement, and every pay supplement and supplement to pay, percentage
-- or shekel, cost-of-living supplements among them, that existed on
-- 31.12.2022 and is counted for the hour value — save (א) one not paid by
-- the month, week or day; (ב) one not updated by the cost-of-living
-- agreements that has another mechanism of update (¶2: one updated at the
-- rates of the frameworks' cost frame counts as having none, and is in the
-- base); (ג) topping up to the minimum wage; (ד) the 2023 shekel, hourly or
-- daily supplement.
@desc A pay component, as far as §29 asks.
DECLARE `2024 percentage base component` HAS
    `existed on 31.12.2022` IS A BOOLEAN
    `counted for the hour value` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid by the month, week or day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `updated by the cost-of-living agreements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has another mechanism of update` IS A BOOLEAN
    `updated at the frameworks' cost-frame rates` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a minimum-wage top-up` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a 2023 shekel, hourly or daily supplement` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:art_29 akn:art_29__para_a akn:art_29__para_b akn:art_29__para_b/p2 akn:art_29__para_c akn:art_29__para_d
GIVEN c IS A `2024 percentage base component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the base of the 2024 percentage supplement` c IF
        c's `existed on 31.12.2022`
    AND c's `counted for the hour value`
    AND c's `paid by the month, week or day`
    AND NOT `excluded by 29(ב)`
    AND NOT c's `a minimum-wage top-up`
    AND NOT c's `a 2023 shekel, hourly or daily supplement`
    WHERE
        `excluded by 29(ב)` MEANS
                NOT c's `updated by the cost-of-living agreements`
            AND c's `has another mechanism of update`
            AND NOT c's `updated at the frameworks' cost-frame rates`

-- A supplement updated at the frameworks' rates is in the base (¶2).
#ASSERT `in the base of the 2024 percentage supplement` (`2024 percentage base component` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `in the base of the 2024 percentage supplement` (`2024 percentage base component` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- §30: so it is no base for the supplements of 31.12.2022, which are in
-- its own base.
@ref akn:art_30
`the 2024 percentage supplement is a base for the supplements of 31.12.2022` MEANS FALSE

GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the base by §29` IS A NUMBER, `the last 1% goes by default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2024 percentage supplement on` d `the base by §29` `the last 1% goes by default` IS
    `the base by §29` TIMES `the 2024 percentage supplement rate on` d `the last 1% goes by default`

#ASSERT `the 2024 percentage supplement on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2025) 10000 TRUE EQUALS 350

-- §31: it is not counted for topping up to the minimum wage. §32: it is
-- salary for every purpose, as §20 says of the shekel supplement. §33: it
-- is counted in the annual supplements and grants computed on the
-- hour-value salary or the budgetary pension's determining salary. §34:
-- and, by §8 of the Pensions Law, in the determining salary.
@ref akn:art_31 akn:art_32 akn:art_34
GIVEN p IS A `what the 2023 framework's payments might count for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2024 percentage supplement counts for` p IF
    NOT (   p EQUALS `topping up to the minimum wage under the 2023 framework`
         OR p EQUALS `the base of the supplements of the eve under the 2023 framework`
         OR p EQUALS `percentage supplements under the 2023 framework`
         OR p EQUALS `unused sick days under the 2023 framework`
         OR p EQUALS `vacation redemption under the 2023 framework`)

@ref akn:art_33
`the 2024 percentage supplement is in the annual supplements on the hour-value or determining salary` MEANS TRUE

-- §35: the payments of ו(1) — §§27–34 — are paid from the salary for
-- December 2024, at the latest from January 2025's; "if from January's,
-- with it the differences for 1.1.2025 to 31.1.2025". Every other such
-- clause (§§24, 26, 36–38, 43, 44, 46) pays the month the pulse starts in;
-- January 2025 is the month the late start itself pays, and the month left
-- unpaid is December 2024. F-framework-2023-a: read as December's
-- differences (convention reading.misprint).
@ref akn:art_35
`the payments of ו(1)` MEANS `2023 pulse payment` (`the 2023 framework's month` 2024 12) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2025 1) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2025 1)
`the payments of ו(1), as read` MEANS `2023 pulse payment` (`the 2023 framework's month` 2024 12) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2025 1) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2024 12)

`§35 pays the differences of the month a late start pays anyway` MEANS
        NOT `a late start pays the pulse's own first month` `the payments of ו(1)`
    AND `the payments of ו(1)`'s `the month whose differences a late start pays` EQUALS `the payments of ו(1)`'s `the latest salary month to start paying it`
    AND `a late start pays the pulse's own first month` `the payments of ו(1), as read`

#ASSERT `§35 pays the differences of the month a late start pays anyway`

`paying the 2024 percentage supplement` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the 2024 percentage supplement from the December 2024 salary`
    LEST  (PARTY `the employer`
           MUST  `pay the 2024 percentage supplement's December differences with the January salary`)

-- §36 ¶2, §37 ¶2, §38 ¶3: each rise is paid from the salary for April of
-- its year, at the latest from May's, with April's differences.
@ref akn:art_36/p2 akn:art_37/p2 akn:art_38/p3
`the payments of the rise of 1.4.2025` MEANS `2023 pulse payment` (`the 2023 framework's month` 2025 4) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2025 5) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2025 4)
`the payments of the rise of 1.4.2026` MEANS `2023 pulse payment` (`the 2023 framework's month` 2026 4) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2026 5) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2026 4)
`the payments of the rise of 1.4.2027` MEANS `2023 pulse payment` (`the 2023 framework's month` 2027 4) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2027 5) (`the 2023 framework's month` 2027 4)

#ASSERT all `a late start pays the pulse's own first month` (LIST `the payments of the rise of 1.4.2025`, `the payments of the rise of 1.4.2026`, `the payments of the rise of 1.4.2027`)

`paying the 2024 percentage supplement's rises` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the 2024 percentage supplement's rise from the April salary`
    LEST  (PARTY `the employer`
           MUST  `pay the 2024 percentage supplement's April differences with the May salary`)

§§ `ז הקדמת הגדלת תוספות צמודות מדד (39–40)`

-- akn:chp_7 The heading of chapter ז.
-- akn:art_39/p7 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.

-- §39: as no new cost-of-living supplements were agreed for over a decade,
-- a pay supplement set to be updated by the change in the index on the
-- days a cost-of-living supplement is paid is updated so: from 1.12.2024 by
-- 2% of its base; from 1.4.2025 to 3.5%; from 1.4.2026 to 5%; from
-- 1.4.2027 to 6% — "בסיס התוספת" being its sum on the eve of the signing
-- (¶6). The steps are the 2024 percentage supplement's, the last one not
-- conditioned on §50.
@ref akn:art_39 akn:art_39/p2 akn:art_39/p3 akn:art_39/p4 akn:art_39/p5 akn:art_39/p6
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the base of the supplement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `an index-linked supplement brought forward in 2023 on` d `the base of the supplement` IS
    `the base of the supplement` `increased by` (`the 2024 percentage supplement rate on` d TRUE)

#ASSERT `an index-linked supplement brought forward in 2023 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2027) 200 EQUALS 212
#ASSERT `an index-linked supplement brought forward in 2023 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2024) 200 EQUALS 200

-- §40: the rise is an advance of the update the supplement's own agreement
-- requires, taken into account on the next update days, so the supplement
-- is never updated twice.
@ref akn:art_40
GIVEN `the index update its agreement requires` IS A NUMBER, `the advance under §39` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what an index update adds after §39's advance` `the index update its agreement requires` `the advance under §39` IS
    `not below zero` (`the index update its agreement requires` MINUS `the advance under §39`)

#ASSERT `what an index update adds after §39's advance` 15 12 EQUALS 3

§§ `ח עובדים בדירוגים ייחודיים (41)`

-- akn:chp_8 The heading of chapter ח.

-- §41: the pay of the unique scales is updated by annex ו' and subject to
-- it; they have neither the 2023 shekel supplement nor the 2024 percentage
-- supplement of chapters ה and ו, save as annex ו' sets. ¶2: "דירוגים
-- ייחודיים" are, in the State's service, (א) the border crossings, (ב) the
-- judges' typists, (ג) Yahalom, (ד) the Israel Land Authority, (ה) Pitzuach,
-- (ו) the legal assistants; and (ז) the social workers.
@ref akn:art_41 akn:art_41/p2 akn:art_41__para_a akn:art_41__para_b akn:art_41__para_c akn:art_41__para_d akn:art_41__para_e akn:art_41__para_f akn:art_41__para_g
`the unique scales of the 2023 framework` MEANS
    LIST "מעברי הגבול", "קלדניות שופטים", "יהלום", "רשות מקרקעי ישראל", "פיצו\"ח", "עוזרים משפטיים", "עובדים סוציאליים"

#ASSERT count `the unique scales of the 2023 framework` EQUALS 7

§§ `ט–י עובדים בשכר שעה ובשכר יומי (42–46)`

-- akn:chp_9 The heading of chapter ט: employees paid by the hour.
-- akn:chp_10 The heading of chapter י: an employee paid by the day.
-- akn:art_43 The heading of §43: the general hourly employee.
-- akn:art_43__para_c/p3 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.

-- §42: the students' scale, paid by the collective agreement of 18.4.2016
-- on the students' pay structure ("הסכם הסטודנטים"), has neither the 2023
-- shekel nor the 2024 percentage supplement of chapters ה and ו; the
-- collective agreement on the students' pay signed alongside this one
-- applies to them. That agreement is not in the corpus: what it gives a
-- student is a named input.
@ref akn:art_42
GIVEN `what the students' agreement of 2023 gives` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a student's 2023 supplement` `what the students' agreement of 2023 gives` IS
    `what the students' agreement of 2023 gives`

-- §43 (א): one paid by the hour whom the agreement covers, save a student,
-- has from 1.7.2023 a shekel supplement for every hour worked ("תוספת
-- שקלית שעתית 2023") of 2.2, and not the monthly 2023 shekel supplement;
-- (ג) from 1.10.2024 it grows by 0.58.
@ref akn:art_43__para_a akn:art_43__para_c
`the 2023 hourly shekel supplement` MEANS 2.2
`the 2023 hourly shekel supplement's rise` MEANS 0.58

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2023 hourly shekel supplement on` d IS
    IF NOT d `is on or after` `the 2023 shekel supplement starts on`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF d `is on or after` `the 2023 shekel supplement grows on`
         THEN `the 2023 hourly shekel supplement` PLUS `the 2023 hourly shekel supplement's rise`
         ELSE `the 2023 hourly shekel supplement`

#ASSERT `the 2023 hourly shekel supplement on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2024) EQUALS 2.78
#ASSERT `the 2023 hourly shekel supplement on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2023) EQUALS 2.2

GIVEN `hours worked` IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2023 hourly shekel supplement for` `hours worked` `hours on` d IS
    `hours worked` TIMES `the 2023 hourly shekel supplement on` d

-- (א) ¶2 and (ג) ¶2: paid from the salary for July 2023 (and for October
-- 2024 the rise), at the latest from the next month's, with the first
-- month's differences.
@ref akn:art_43__para_a/p2
`paying the 2023 hourly shekel supplement` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the 2023 hourly shekel supplement from the July 2023 salary`

@ref akn:art_43__para_c/p2
`paying the 2023 hourly shekel supplement's rise` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the 2023 hourly shekel supplement's rise from the October 2024 salary`

-- (ב) and §45: §§19–22 — not for the minimum wage, salary for every
-- purpose, no base for the supplements of the eve, updated by the
-- cost-of-living rates after the period — apply to the hourly and the
-- daily supplements too.
@ref akn:art_43__para_b akn:art_45
GIVEN p IS A `what the 2023 framework's payments might count for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2023 hourly or daily shekel supplement counts for` p IF
    `the 2023 shekel supplement counts for` p

-- §44: one paid by the day whom the agreement covers has from 1.7.2023 a
-- daily shekel supplement for every day worked ("תוספת שקלית יומית 2023")
-- of 19.2 at a five-day workplace or 16 at a six-day one, and not the
-- monthly supplement; §46: from 1.10.2024 it grows by 4.8 (to 24) or by 4
-- (to 20).
@ref akn:art_44 akn:art_46
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `a five-day workplace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2023 daily shekel supplement on` d `a five-day workplace` IS
    IF NOT d `is on or after` `the 2023 shekel supplement starts on`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `a five-day workplace`
         THEN (IF d `is on or after` `the 2023 shekel supplement grows on` THEN 19.2 PLUS 4.8 ELSE 19.2)
         ELSE (IF d `is on or after` `the 2023 shekel supplement grows on` THEN 16 PLUS 4 ELSE 16)

#ASSERT `the 2023 daily shekel supplement on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2024) TRUE EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `the 2023 daily shekel supplement on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2024) FALSE EQUALS 20

-- The daily sums are the monthly ones over the days §12(ג) counts in a
-- month — 20.83 at a five-day workplace, 25 at a six-day one — to within
-- ten agorot a month: 19.2 × 20.83 = 399.94, 16 × 25 = 400, 24 × 20.83 =
-- 499.92, 20 × 25 = 500.
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `a five-day workplace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a month of the 2023 daily shekel supplement on` d `a five-day workplace` IS
    `the 2023 daily shekel supplement on` d `a five-day workplace` TIMES (IF `a five-day workplace` THEN 20.83 ELSE 25)

#ASSERT `a month of the 2023 daily shekel supplement on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2023) FALSE EQUALS `the 2023 shekel supplement for a full position on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2023) FALSE
#ASSERT `a month of the 2023 daily shekel supplement on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2024) FALSE EQUALS `the 2023 shekel supplement for a full position on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2024) FALSE
#ASSERT `the 2023 shekel supplement for a full position on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2023) FALSE MINUS `a month of the 2023 daily shekel supplement on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2023) TRUE LESS THAN 0.1
#ASSERT `the 2023 shekel supplement for a full position on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2024) FALSE MINUS `a month of the 2023 daily shekel supplement on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2024) TRUE LESS THAN 0.1

@ref akn:art_44/p2
`paying the 2023 daily shekel supplement` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the 2023 daily shekel supplement from the July 2023 salary`

@ref akn:art_46/p2
`paying the 2023 daily shekel supplement's rise` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the 2023 daily shekel supplement's rise from the October 2024 salary`

§§ `יא הוראות מיוחדות לעובדים המקבלים שכר לפי שכר עובדי הוראה (47–49)`

-- akn:chp_11 The heading of chapter יא.
-- akn:art_47 The heading of §47: "in this chapter".
-- akn:art_48/p2 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.

-- §47: "עובדים אשר מקבלים שכר לפי שכר עובדי הוראה" are (א) the employees
-- of the Ministry of Education's settlement-education administration paid
-- by the teaching employees' scale under the agreement of 15.8.1978; (ב)
-- those of the local authorities' youth, society and community education
-- scale paid by the teaching employees' salary under the agreement of
-- 14.9.1987; (ג) other employees of the State the Histadrut represents
-- paid by that salary, whose names are in a document the parties keep; an
-- error in that list goes to the follow-up committee at the request of the
-- Histadrut's chairman or the wages commissioner.
DECLARE `2023 teachers'-salary group` IS ONE OF
    `settlement education under the agreement of 15.8.1978`
    `youth, society and community education under the agreement of 14.9.1987`
    `State employees on the parties' list paid by the teachers' salary`

@ref akn:art_47/p1 akn:art_47__para_a akn:art_47__para_b akn:art_47__para_c
`the groups chapter יא of 2023 reaches` MEANS
    LIST `settlement education under the agreement of 15.8.1978`,
         `youth, society and community education under the agreement of 14.9.1987`,
         `State employees on the parties' list paid by the teachers' salary`

`raising an error in the teachers'-salary list` MEANS
    PARTY `the wages commissioner`
    MAY   `raise an error in the list of employees paid by the teachers' salary`

-- §48: they have no double cost for the same time, under this agreement
-- and under the linkage to the teaching employees' salary: they have the
-- 2023 shekel supplement (chapter ה) and the 2024 percentage supplement
-- (chapter ו) on the days and at the sums and rates set there, and from
-- them is set off every pay supplement paid, or to be paid, for the time
-- from 1.1.2020 to the end of this agreement's period by the linkage to
-- the teaching employees' salary — on the days and at the sums and rates
-- the linkage pays it — and no more than the two supplements' full sum at
-- that time. ¶3: the section neither makes nor takes away a right to the
-- linkage.
@ref akn:art_48
`the linkage set off from the 2023 supplements runs from` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020

GIVEN `the framework's two supplements` IS A NUMBER, `the linkage's rises for 1.1.2020 on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what the 2023 framework adds for one paid by the teachers' salary` `the framework's two supplements` `the linkage's rises for 1.1.2020 on` IS
    `the framework's two supplements` MINUS min `the linkage's rises for 1.1.2020 on` `the framework's two supplements`

-- What he has in all, from both: the larger of the two.
GIVEN `the framework's two supplements` IS A NUMBER, `the linkage's rises for 1.1.2020 on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what one paid by the teachers' salary has from both` `the framework's two supplements` `the linkage's rises for 1.1.2020 on` IS
    `the linkage's rises for 1.1.2020 on` PLUS `what the 2023 framework adds for one paid by the teachers' salary` `the framework's two supplements` `the linkage's rises for 1.1.2020 on`

#ASSERT `what the 2023 framework adds for one paid by the teachers' salary` 500 300 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `what the 2023 framework adds for one paid by the teachers' salary` 500 800 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `what one paid by the teachers' salary has from both` 500 300 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `what one paid by the teachers' salary has from both` 500 800 EQUALS 800

@ref akn:art_48/p3
`chapter יא of 2023 makes or takes away a right to the teachers' linkage` MEANS FALSE

-- §49: chapters ט and י compute a pay supplement for those paid by the
-- hour and the day; they are no approval or consent of the Histadrut to
-- employment by the hour or the day.
@ref akn:art_49
`chapters ט and י of 2023 approve employment by the hour or the day` MEANS FALSE

§§ `יב משא ומתן נוסף (50–58)`

-- akn:chp_12 The heading of chapter יב.
-- akn:art_55 The heading of §55: negotiating to narrow the minimum-wage top-up.
-- akn:art_55/p3 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.
-- akn:art_56 The heading of §56: negotiating the structure of employment.

-- §50: a cost equal to 1% of §29's base is allocated, for the employees the
-- 2024 percentage supplement reaches, divided by the default of ו'3 (§38)
-- or as a collective agreement between the parties signed by 31.1.2027
-- divides it. §52: §§50 and 51 do not reach the unique scales, those paid
-- by the hour or the day, or those paid by the teaching employees' salary,
-- who have arrangements of their own.
@ref akn:art_50 akn:art_52
`the cost §50 of 2023 allocates` MEANS 1%

GIVEN b IS A `2023 framework pay basis`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§50 of 2023 reaches` b IF
        `chapter ו of 2023 reaches` b
    AND NOT (   b EQUALS `paid by the hour under the 2023 framework`
             OR b EQUALS `paid by the day under the 2023 framework`
             OR b EQUALS `paid by the teaching employees' salary under the 2023 framework`)

#ASSERT `§50 of 2023 reaches` `paid monthly under the 2023 framework`
#ASSERT NOT `§50 of 2023 reaches` `paid by the teaching employees' salary under the 2023 framework`

-- The default's 1% is §38's step.
#ASSERT `the 2024 percentage supplement rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2027) TRUE MINUS `the 2024 percentage supplement rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2027) FALSE EQUALS `the cost §50 of 2023 allocates`

-- For an employee §50 does not reach, §38 applies without its condition:
-- `the last 1% goes by default` is TRUE for him.
GIVEN b IS A `2023 framework pay basis`, `an agreement under §50 signed by 31.1.2027` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the last 1% of 2023 goes by default for` b `an agreement under §50 signed by 31.1.2027` IF
    NOT (`§50 of 2023 reaches` b AND `an agreement under §50 signed by 31.1.2027`)

-- §51: by 1.11.2026 the employers negotiate with each union another
-- division of §50's cost for the employees negotiated for.
@ref akn:art_51
`the 2023 framework's last day to negotiate the last 1%` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2026

`negotiating the last 1% of 2023` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `negotiate another division of the last 1% of the 2023 framework`

-- §53: each employer gives the Histadrut the salary data it holds that bear
-- on the negotiation and that it asks for, by law (the Privacy Protection
-- Law among them; no identifying details); ¶2: as it holds them,
-- unprocessed; ¶3: a request that needs processing the employer finds
-- reasonable it examines favourably, tells the Histadrut the estimated
-- cost, and produces the data if the Histadrut agrees to bear it;
-- otherwise the request goes no further.
@ref akn:art_53 akn:art_53/p2
`transferring the salary data under the 2023 framework` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `transfer the salary data the Histadrut asks for under the 2023 framework`

@ref akn:art_53/p3
GIVEN `the processing is reasonable to the employer` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Histadrut bears the cost` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `processed data is produced under the 2023 framework` `the processing is reasonable to the employer` `the Histadrut bears the cost` IF
    `the processing is reasonable to the employer` AND `the Histadrut bears the cost`

-- §54: §§50–51 take nothing from industrial peace (chapter כב); absent
-- another agreement by 31.1.2027 the cost goes by ו'3; and no dispute is
-- declared, and no organisational measure taken, for want of agreement on
-- the allocation.
@ref akn:art_54
`no dispute for want of agreement on the last 1%` MEANS
    PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
    SHANT `declare a dispute for want of agreement on allocating the last 1%`

-- §55: the parties negotiate changing how the 2024 percentage supplement's
-- pulses are paid, all or some, to narrow the minimum-wage top-up, at no
-- change in cost; absent another agreement it is paid as this agreement
-- says; ¶2: subject to the exhaustion of claims and industrial peace. §56:
-- the discussions on the structure of employment go on; ¶2: the parties
-- recognise the importance of better service and say they will cooperate
-- in the effort. §57: each party keeps its claims on §§55 and 56. §58: for
-- an employer under §29 of the Budget Foundations Law, the chapter is
-- subject to §29.
@ref akn:art_55/p1 akn:art_55/p2
`negotiating the 2024 pulses for the minimum wage` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `negotiate the 2024 percentage supplement's pulses to narrow the minimum-wage top-up`

`a change of the 2024 pulses may change their cost` MEANS FALSE

@ref akn:art_56/p1 akn:art_56/p2
`discussing the structure of employment under the 2023 framework` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `go on discussing the structure of employment under the 2023 framework`

@ref akn:art_57
`each party keeps its claims on §§55–56 of 2023` MEANS TRUE

@ref akn:art_58
`chapter יב of 2023 is subject to §29 of the Budget Foundations Law` MEANS TRUE

§§ `יג הגדלת תוספות מיוחדות (59–61)`

-- akn:chp_13 The heading of chapter יג.
-- akn:art_61 The heading of §61.
-- akn:art_61/p3 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.

-- §59: a pay supplement that meets (א)–(ה) together is a "תוספת מיוחדת":
-- (א) it is not counted for the hour value; (ב) it is not affected by the
-- hour value and not updated with the pension's determining salary; (ג) it
-- is paid by the month, week or day; (ד) it is updated by the
-- cost-of-living agreements and has no other mechanism; (ה) it is no
-- minimum-wage top-up. ¶2: an expense reimbursement of any kind is none.
@desc A pay supplement, as far as §59 asks.
DECLARE `2023 special supplement candidate` HAS
    `counted for the hour value under 2023` IS A BOOLEAN
    `affected by the hour value or the determining salary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid by the month, week or day under 2023` IS A BOOLEAN
    `updated by the cost-of-living agreements alone` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a minimum-wage top-up under 2023` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an expense reimbursement` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:art_59 akn:art_59__para_a akn:art_59__para_b akn:art_59__para_c akn:art_59__para_d akn:art_59__para_e akn:art_59/p2
GIVEN s IS A `2023 special supplement candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a special supplement of 2023` s IF
        NOT s's `counted for the hour value under 2023`
    AND NOT s's `affected by the hour value or the determining salary`
    AND s's `paid by the month, week or day under 2023`
    AND s's `updated by the cost-of-living agreements alone`
    AND NOT s's `a minimum-wage top-up under 2023`
    AND NOT s's `an expense reimbursement`

-- §60: each is updated from 1.12.2024 by 2% of its base sum, from 1.4.2025
-- to 3.5%, from 1.4.2026 to 5% and from 1.4.2027 to 6% — "סכום הבסיס" being
-- its sum paid on the eve of the signing by the wages commissioner's
-- circulars. The steps are §39's.
@ref akn:art_60 akn:art_60__para_a akn:art_60__para_b akn:art_60__para_c akn:art_60__para_d akn:art_60/p2 akn:art_60/p3
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the base sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a special supplement of 2023 on` d `the base sum` IS
    `an index-linked supplement brought forward in 2023 on` d `the base sum`

#ASSERT `a special supplement of 2023 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2026) 1000 EQUALS 1050

-- §61: a supplement set to be updated at the frameworks' cost-frame rates
-- is not updated: it was counted in §29's base and in setting the 2023
-- shekel supplement, which is deemed to apply its update; ¶2: this
-- prevails over every earlier provision, whatever its source.
@ref akn:art_61/p1 akn:art_61/p2
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the supplement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a supplement updated at the frameworks' rates, under the 2023 framework on` d `the supplement` IS
    `the supplement`

#ASSERT `a supplement updated at the frameworks' rates, under the 2023 framework on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2027) 300 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `in the base of the 2024 percentage supplement` (`2024 percentage base component` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `יד(1) קיצור שבוע העבודה (62–75)`

-- akn:chp_14 The heading of chapter יד: productivity and excellence in the public sector.
