-- §62(א): the shorter week (sub-chapter יד(1), §§62–75) reaches only (1)
-- those whose week on the eve of the signing, for a full position, is over
-- 40 hours and at most 42 ("משרה מלאה שבועית"), and part-time employees
-- measured on such a position; (2) those paid by the hour whose rights,
-- computed in proportion to a position on the eve, are computed on a
-- position of over 173.333 hours a month and at most 182 ("עובד שעתי").
-- ¶2: not one the Hours of Work and Rest Law does not reach by its §30(א);
-- whether such a one meeting (1) or (2) is entitled goes to the follow-up
-- committee on the written request of the Histadrut's chairman. ¶3: such
-- an employee is "עובד" in the sub-chapter.
@desc An employee, as far as sub-chapter יד(1) asks.
DECLARE `2023 week employee` HAS
    `paid by the hour for the shorter week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the full-time week on the eve, in hours` IS A NUMBER
    `the monthly hours his rights were computed on, on the eve` IS A NUMBER
    `outside the Hours of Work and Rest Law by its §30(א)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a firefighter on 24-hour shifts` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:art_62__para_a akn:art_62__para_a__subpara_1 akn:art_62__para_a__subpara_2 akn:art_62__para_a__subpara_2/p2 akn:art_62__para_a__subpara_2/p3 akn:art_62__para_c
GIVEN e IS A `2023 week employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the shorter week of 2023 reaches` e IF
        NOT e's `outside the Hours of Work and Rest Law by its §30(א)`
    AND NOT e's `a firefighter on 24-hour shifts`
    AND (IF e's `paid by the hour for the shorter week`
         THEN e's `the monthly hours his rights were computed on, on the eve` `is above` 173.333
              AND e's `the monthly hours his rights were computed on, on the eve` AT MOST 182
         ELSE e's `the full-time week on the eve, in hours` `is above` 40
              AND e's `the full-time week on the eve, in hours` AT MOST 42)

#ASSERT `the shorter week of 2023 reaches` (`2023 week employee` FALSE 42 0 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the shorter week of 2023 reaches` (`2023 week employee` FALSE 40 0 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the shorter week of 2023 reaches` (`2023 week employee` FALSE 43 0 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the shorter week of 2023 reaches` (`2023 week employee` TRUE 0 182 FALSE FALSE)

-- (ב): the sub-chapter neither takes away nor adds legal claims on the week
-- of those who worked over 42 hours on the eve. (ג): the firefighters on
-- 24-hour shifts are outside it; the State and the Histadrut negotiate an
-- arrangement economically equivalent (by the pulses' days, even if signed
-- later), with an effort to finish by March 2024. (ד): for the Histadrut's
-- employees in the defence plants, the parties sign a follow-up decision
-- within a week of the signing on how the sub-chapter applies to them.
@ref akn:art_62__para_b
`the shorter week of 2023 bears on the claims of those over 42 hours` MEANS FALSE

`negotiating the firefighters' equivalent of the shorter week` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `negotiate an equivalent arrangement for the firefighters' 24-hour shifts`

@ref akn:art_62__para_d
`signing the defence plants' follow-up decision on the shorter week` MEANS
    PARTY `the follow-up committee`
    MUST  `sign a follow-up decision on the defence plants' shorter week within a week`

-- The hours of a week and of a month, the month being 182/42 weeks: 42
-- hours and 182, then 41 and 177.667, then 40 and 173.333 (§§63(ב)(1)–(2),
-- 67, 69).
`the weeks in a month of the shorter week` MEANS 182 DIVIDED BY 42

#ASSERT (41 TIMES `the weeks in a month of the shorter week`) `to the nearest` 0.001 EQUALS 177.667
#ASSERT (40 TIMES `the weeks in a month of the shorter week`) `to the nearest` 0.001 EQUALS 173.333

-- §63(א): the week of one employed in a full-time week is shortened to 40
-- hours from 1 September 2024, with no cut in pay for it ("הקיצור
-- ההסכמי"). (ב): in two pulses — the first from 1.10.2023, at the latest
-- from 1.11.2023; the second from 1.9.2024, but at an employer whose first
-- pulse was from 1.11.2023 (not 1.10.2023), from 1.8.2024 ("הפעימות").
@ref akn:art_63__para_a akn:art_63__para_a/p2 akn:art_63__para_b akn:art_63__para_b/p2 akn:art_63__para_b/p3 akn:art_63__para_b/p4
`the first pulse of 2023 opens on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2023
`the first pulse of 2023 at the latest` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2023

GIVEN `the employer's first pulse` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the second pulse of 2023 at an employer whose first was` `the employer's first pulse` IS
    IF `the employer's first pulse` EQUALS `the first pulse of 2023 at the latest`
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2024
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2024

#ASSERT `the second pulse of 2023 at an employer whose first was` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2023) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2024
#ASSERT `the second pulse of 2023 at an employer whose first was` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2023) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2024

-- (1) from the first pulse, for one employed 42 hours a week, a quarter of
-- an hour off each of Sunday to Wednesday — up to a quarter at a workplace
-- of over 41 and under 42 — so the week is 41 hours and the month 177.667
-- ("הימים המקוצרים"); where the short day by the 2018 extension order is
-- not Thursday, the four days that are not it ("הימים המקוצרים האחרים").
-- (2) from the second, another quarter of an hour on those days — up to a
-- quarter at a workplace of over 40 and under 41 — so the week is 40 and
-- the month 173.333 ("קיצור ברירת המחדל").
@ref akn:art_63__para_b__subpara_1 akn:art_63__para_b__subpara_2 akn:art_63__para_b__subpara_2/p2
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the employer's first pulse` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the full-time week of 2023 in hours on` d `the employer's first pulse` IS
    IF d `is on or after` (`the second pulse of 2023 at an employer whose first was` `the employer's first pulse`)
    THEN 40
    ELSE IF d `is on or after` `the employer's first pulse`
         THEN 41
         ELSE 42

GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the employer's first pulse` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the full-time month of 2023 in hours on` d `the employer's first pulse` IS
    (`the full-time week of 2023 in hours on` d `the employer's first pulse` TIMES `the weeks in a month of the shorter week`) `to the nearest` 0.001

#ASSERT `the full-time month of 2023 in hours on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 10 2023) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2023) EQUALS 177.667
#ASSERT `the full-time month of 2023 in hours on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 8 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2023) EQUALS 173.333
#ASSERT `the full-time month of 2023 in hours on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 8 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2023) EQUALS 177.667

-- A quarter of an hour on each of four days is the hour a pulse takes off.
`the quarter hours a pulse of 2023 takes off a 42-hour week` MEANS 4 TIMES 0.25
#ASSERT `the quarter hours a pulse of 2023 takes off a 42-hour week` EQUALS 42 MINUS 41

GIVEN `the week on the eve` IS A NUMBER, `the week the pulse brings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what a pulse of 2023 takes off a day` `the week on the eve` `the week the pulse brings` IS
    min 0.25 (`not below zero` ((`the week on the eve` MINUS `the week the pulse brings`) DIVIDED BY 4))

#ASSERT `what a pulse of 2023 takes off a day` 42 41 EQUALS 0.25
#ASSERT `what a pulse of 2023 takes off a day` 41.5 41 EQUALS 0.125

`shortening the week` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `shorten the working week`

-- §64(א): an employer may change how the agreed shortening is made — an
-- alternative to the default, no day shortened by more than an hour — on
-- all these terms: (1) for the needs of the work, operational ones among
-- them; (2) the week's shortenings sum to the default's of §63(ב), on the
-- same pulse days; (3) no more than half an hour on the day the employer
-- chose to shorten under the 2018 extension order on the shorter week; (4)
-- the employees are told; (5) their requests and needs are weighed as far
-- as possible; (6) a report goes first to the wages commissioner and the
-- Histadrut; (7) and the change waits for the wages commissioner's
-- approval; (8) the Histadrut's claims of abuse go to the follow-up
-- committee at the request of the trade-union division's chairman.
@desc A proposed alternative to the default shortening.
DECLARE `2023 alternative shortening` HAS
    `for the needs of the work` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day's longest shortening, in hours` IS A NUMBER
    `the week's shortenings, in hours` IS A NUMBER
    `the default's week of shortenings, in hours` IS A NUMBER
    `the shortening on the extension order's day, in hours` IS A NUMBER
    `the employees were told` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reported to the wages commissioner and the Histadrut` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the wages commissioner approved it` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:art_64__para_a akn:art_64__para_a__subpara_1 akn:art_64__para_a__subpara_2 akn:art_64__para_a__subpara_3 akn:art_64__para_a__subpara_4 akn:art_64__para_a__subpara_5 akn:art_64__para_a__subpara_6 akn:art_64__para_a__subpara_7
GIVEN s IS A `2023 alternative shortening`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an employer may shorten the 2023 week otherwise` s IF
        s's `for the needs of the work`
    AND s's `the day's longest shortening, in hours` AT MOST 1
    AND s's `the week's shortenings, in hours` EQUALS s's `the default's week of shortenings, in hours`
    AND s's `the shortening on the extension order's day, in hours` AT MOST 0.5
    AND s's `the employees were told`
    AND s's `reported to the wages commissioner and the Histadrut`
    AND s's `the wages commissioner approved it`

#ASSERT `an employer may shorten the 2023 week otherwise` (`2023 alternative shortening` TRUE 1 2 2 0.5 TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `an employer may shorten the 2023 week otherwise` (`2023 alternative shortening` TRUE 1 2 2 0.5 TRUE TRUE FALSE)

`changing how the week is shortened` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MAY   `change how the week is shortened`

`weighing the employees' requests in changing the shortening` MEANS TRUE

@ref akn:art_64__para_a__subpara_8
`the Histadrut's claims of abuse of §64 go to the follow-up committee` MEANS TRUE

-- (ב): from 1.1.2025 how the shortening is applied is fixed, and changes
-- only by the follow-up committee (chapter כג) or by the parties' consent
-- with the wages commissioner's approval.
@ref akn:art_64__para_b
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `by the follow-up committee or approved consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2023 shortening may be changed on` d `by the follow-up committee or approved consent` IF
    (NOT d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2025)) OR `by the follow-up committee or approved consent`

#ASSERT NOT `the 2023 shortening may be changed on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2025) FALSE

-- §65(א): a part-time employee's week is shortened with no cut in pay, his
-- hours in proportion to his position of a full week of 41 or 40 hours
-- instead of 42 or 41, by the pulses. ¶2–¶5: half a position, 21 hours a
-- week before the first pulse, 20.5 after it, 20 after the second.
@ref akn:art_65__para_a akn:art_65__para_a/p2 akn:art_65__para_a/p3 akn:art_65__para_a/p4 akn:art_65__para_a/p5
GIVEN `position share` IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE, `the employer's first pulse` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a part-time week of 2023` `position share` d `the employer's first pulse` IS
    `position share` TIMES `the full-time week of 2023 in hours on` d `the employer's first pulse`

#ASSERT `a part-time week of 2023` (50%) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2023) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2023) EQUALS 21
#ASSERT `a part-time week of 2023` (50%) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2023) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2023) EQUALS 20.5
#ASSERT `a part-time week of 2023` (50%) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2023) EQUALS 20

-- (ב): notwithstanding (א), where the work needs it, weighing the
-- employees' requests, an employer may keep a part-time employee's hours as
-- they were on the eve, raising his position share, and tells him the new
-- share. ¶2–¶3: one at 50% (91 of 182 hours a month) who goes on working
-- 91 hours has 51.22% after the first pulse and 52.5% after the second.
@ref akn:art_65__para_b akn:art_65__para_b/p2 akn:art_65__para_b/p3
GIVEN `monthly hours kept` IS A NUMBER, `the full-time month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position share that keeps the hours` `monthly hours kept` `the full-time month` IS
    (`monthly hours kept` DIVIDED BY `the full-time month`) `to the nearest` 0.0001

#ASSERT `the position share that keeps the hours` 91 177.667 EQUALS 51.22%
#ASSERT `the position share that keeps the hours` 91 173.333 EQUALS 52.5%

`telling a part-time employee the updated share` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `tell a part-time employee the updated position share`

-- §66(א): an employee asked to work in the time the shortening took off
-- works as asked and by law, and is paid for it as an overtime hour at the
-- employer. (ב): where work is in shifts the employer sets each shift's
-- hours and arrangements to fit the shortening. (ג): the employer may adjust
-- the ending hour and the arrangements (transport, lunch), and the
-- Histadrut has no further claim on it.
@ref akn:art_66__para_a
`paying the reduced time worked` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay a reduced-time hour worked as an overtime hour`

@ref akn:art_66__para_b akn:art_66__para_c
`the employer sets the shifts and the end of the day to fit the 2023 shortening` MEANS TRUE

-- §67: with the shortening, the hour's value for overtime, stand-by,
-- incentive pay and every component derived from it is computed for one in
-- a full-time week on 177.667 hours a month (41 a week) after the first
-- pulse, and 173.333 (40 a week) after the second — save where an
-- agreement or arrangement computes it more favourably. ¶2: the same value
-- holds for a parallel part-time employee; an hourly one, by §69.
-- ¶3–¶7: components of 7,000: 38.46 an hour on the eve (7,000/182), 39.40
-- after the first pulse, 40.38 after the second.
@ref akn:art_67/p1 akn:art_67/p2
GIVEN `the components of the hour value` IS A NUMBER, `the full-time month` IS A NUMBER, `a more favourable hour value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2023 hour value` `the components of the hour value` `the full-time month` `a more favourable hour value` IS
    max (`the components of the hour value` DIVIDED BY `the full-time month`) `a more favourable hour value`

@ref akn:art_67/p3 akn:art_67/p4 akn:art_67/p5 akn:art_67/p6 akn:art_67/p7
#ASSERT `to the agora` (`the 2023 hour value` 7000 182 0) EQUALS 38.46
#ASSERT `to the agora` (`the 2023 hour value` 7000 177.667 0) EQUALS 39.40
#ASSERT `to the agora` (`the 2023 hour value` 7000 173.333 0) EQUALS 40.38

-- §68 ¶1: if after the signing a law or an extension order shortens the
-- week for employers ("השינוי העתידי"), the more favourable of the two
-- arrangements applies. ¶2: if in the agreement's period a law or order
-- reduces working hours otherwise (actual hours, leave and the like — "צמצום
-- העבודה"), the follow-up committee decides how it is set against the
-- favourable arrangements; this paragraph lapses if the economy's week is
-- shortened to 40 hours.
@ref akn:art_68/p1
GIVEN `the week under this sub-chapter` IS A NUMBER, `the week under the future change` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the week of 2023 after a future change` `the week under this sub-chapter` `the week under the future change` IS
    min `the week under this sub-chapter` `the week under the future change`

@ref akn:art_68/p2
GIVEN `the economy's week is 40 hours` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reduction of 2023's period goes to the follow-up committee` `the economy's week is 40 hours` IF
    NOT `the economy's week is 40 hours`

-- §69 (א): "סטודנט" — the students' scale, paid by the students' agreement,
-- to whom the agreement signed alongside on students' pay applies; "חוק
-- שכר מינימום" — the Minimum Wage Law, 5747-1987. (ב): an hourly employee's
-- rights derived in proportion to a full weekly position (recuperation,
-- clothing and the like) are computed (1) from the first pulse to the eve
-- of the second on 177.667 hours a month, or the basis he had on the eve
-- of the signing, whichever is more favourable; (2) from the second, on
-- 173.333.
@ref akn:art_69__para_a akn:art_69__para_a/p2 akn:art_69__para_a/p3 akn:art_69__para_b akn:art_69__para_b__subpara_1 akn:art_69__para_b__subpara_2
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the employer's first pulse` IS A DATE, `his basis on the eve` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the hours an hourly employee's 2023 rights are computed on` d `the employer's first pulse` `his basis on the eve` IS
    IF d `is on or after` (`the second pulse of 2023 at an employer whose first was` `the employer's first pulse`)
    THEN 173.333
    ELSE IF d `is on or after` `the employer's first pulse`
         THEN min 177.667 `his basis on the eve`
         ELSE `his basis on the eve`

-- A smaller denominator is the more favourable: a right of 1,000 a year for
-- a full position, on 91 hours a month, is more on 177.667 than on 182.
#ASSERT `the hours an hourly employee's 2023 rights are computed on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2023) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2023) 182 EQUALS 177.667
#ASSERT `the hours an hourly employee's 2023 rights are computed on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2023) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2023) 175 EQUALS 175
#ASSERT `the hours an hourly employee's 2023 rights are computed on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2023) 175 EQUALS 173.333

-- (ג): an hourly employee, not a student, whose hour on the signing is
-- worth no more than 105 has his hourly pay raised at each pulse by C =
-- A/B − 1: A the hours his rights were computed on before the shortening,
-- B the hours after it (the first pulse: 177.667 or his eve basis,
-- whichever is more favourable; the second: 173.333); the rise is on his
-- hourly pay as it was on the eve of the pulse; ¶7: where another
-- arrangement (linkage, say) raises it for the shortening too, only the
-- higher rate, never both. The second pulse brings the rise to C, not C on
-- C: example א' gives 5% in all, 52.5 on 50.
@ref akn:art_69__para_c akn:art_69__para_c/p2 akn:art_69__para_c/p3 akn:art_69__para_c/p4 akn:art_69__para_c/p5 akn:art_69__para_c__subpara_1 akn:art_69__para_c__subpara_2 akn:art_69__para_c/p6 akn:art_69__para_c/p7
GIVEN `hours before` IS A NUMBER, `hours after` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `C of the 2023 hourly rise` `hours before` `hours after` IS
    `hours before` DIVIDED BY `hours after` MINUS 1

GIVEN `the hourly pay on the eve of the shortening` IS A NUMBER
      `hours before` IS A NUMBER
      `hours after` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate another arrangement gives` IS A NUMBER
      `a student` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2023 hourly pay after a pulse` `the hourly pay on the eve of the shortening` `hours before` `hours after` `the rate another arrangement gives` `a student` IS
    IF `a student` OR `the hourly pay on the eve of the shortening` `is above` 105
    THEN `the hourly pay on the eve of the shortening` `increased by` `the rate another arrangement gives`
    ELSE `the hourly pay on the eve of the shortening` `increased by` (max (`C of the 2023 hourly rise` `hours before` `hours after`) `the rate another arrangement gives`)

-- Example א' (¶8–¶16): 50 an hour, A = 182: the first pulse 182/177.667 − 1
-- = 2.44% and 51.22; the second 182/173.333 − 1 = 5% and 52.5.
@ref akn:art_69__para_c/p8 akn:art_69__para_c/p9 akn:art_69__para_c/p10 akn:art_69__para_c/p11 akn:art_69__para_c/p12 akn:art_69__para_c/p13 akn:art_69__para_c/p14 akn:art_69__para_c/p15 akn:art_69__para_c/p16
#ASSERT (`C of the 2023 hourly rise` 182 177.667) `to the nearest` 0.0001 EQUALS 2.44%
#ASSERT (`C of the 2023 hourly rise` 182 173.333) `to the nearest` 0.0001 EQUALS 5%
#ASSERT `to the agora` (`the 2023 hourly pay after a pulse` 50 182 177.667 0 FALSE) EQUALS 51.22
#ASSERT `to the agora` (`the 2023 hourly pay after a pulse` 50 182 173.333 0 FALSE) EQUALS 52.5

-- (ד): from each pulse an hourly employee's hourly pay (the components the
-- Minimum Wage Law counts and those it does not, by contract, agreement or
-- arrangement) is the higher of (1) what his terms give and (2) the monthly
-- minimum wage — 5,571.75 on the signing, as updated — divided by 177.667
-- hours from the first pulse and 173.333 from the second, instead of 182.
@ref akn:art_69__para_d akn:art_69__para_d__subpara_1 akn:art_69__para_d__subpara_2
`the monthly minimum wage on the 2023 signing` MEANS 5571.75

GIVEN `the hourly pay by his terms` IS A NUMBER, `the monthly minimum wage` IS A NUMBER, `the full-time month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2023 hourly pay floor` `the hourly pay by his terms` `the monthly minimum wage` `the full-time month` IS
    max `the hourly pay by his terms` (`the monthly minimum wage` DIVIDED BY `the full-time month`)

#ASSERT `to the agora` (`the 2023 hourly pay floor` 30 `the monthly minimum wage on the 2023 signing` 173.333) EQUALS 32.14
#ASSERT `the 2023 hourly pay floor` 40 `the monthly minimum wage on the 2023 signing` 173.333 EQUALS 40

-- (ה): where his hour's value rises by this section, the employer may
-- reduce his hours in step with the rise, keeping what he would have
-- earned without it.
@ref akn:art_69__para_e
GIVEN `hours before` IS A NUMBER, `the hourly pay before` IS A NUMBER, `the hourly pay after` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the fewest hours that keep the 2023 earnings` `hours before` `the hourly pay before` `the hourly pay after` IS
    `hours before` TIMES `the hourly pay before` DIVIDED BY `the hourly pay after`

#ASSERT `the fewest hours that keep the 2023 earnings` 105 50 52.5 EQUALS 100

-- §70(א): definitions. "הסדר צמצום" — an arrangement reducing working hours
-- (other than added vacation, concentrated or sabbatical days, pool hours
-- and clock rounding) as a working parent's, age hours' or holidays'
-- arrangement, not by this agreement but by another norm; and any other
-- arrangement reducing hours unless the follow-up committee decides
-- otherwise — save the arrangements of (ב). "הסדר הורה עובד" — Takshir
-- 31.15 or its parallel, a parent of a child over a year old; "הסדר חג
-- ומועד" — Takshir 32.51 and fast days of 32.53 or their parallels; "הסדר
-- שעות גיל" — fewer hours or absence counted as work by age; "הסדר עיגולי
-- שעון" — absence hours counted as work, set on the eve (parking, a moved
-- workplace, Takshir 91.151's rounding), save (ב)'s; "הסדר שעות מאגר" — a
-- monthly quota of missing hours paid and not counted as missing; "הסדר
-- נסיעות" — travel to a remote workplace counted as work; "הסדרי חניה" —
-- the time to and from parking. ¶10: where by the rules of the eve two
-- reduction arrangements offset each other, the part offset is not counted
-- in their daily or weekly sum.
DECLARE `2023 hours arrangement` IS ONE OF
    `the working parent's arrangement of 2023`
    `the holidays' arrangement of 2023`
    `the age hours' arrangement of 2023`
    `another reduction arrangement of 2023`
    `the clock-rounding arrangement of 2023`
    `the pool hours' arrangement of 2023`
    `the travel arrangement of 2023`
    `added vacation or concentrated days of 2023`

@ref akn:art_70__para_a akn:art_70__para_a/p2 akn:art_70__para_a/p3 akn:art_70__para_a/p4 akn:art_70__para_a/p5 akn:art_70__para_a/p6 akn:art_70__para_a/p7 akn:art_70__para_a/p8 akn:art_70__para_a/p9
GIVEN a IS A `2023 hours arrangement`, `the follow-up committee decided otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reduction arrangement of 2023` a `the follow-up committee decided otherwise` IF
        a EQUALS `the working parent's arrangement of 2023`
    OR  a EQUALS `the holidays' arrangement of 2023`
    OR  a EQUALS `the age hours' arrangement of 2023`
    OR  (a EQUALS `another reduction arrangement of 2023` AND NOT `the follow-up committee decided otherwise`)

#ASSERT NOT `a reduction arrangement of 2023` `the clock-rounding arrangement of 2023` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `a reduction arrangement of 2023` `the pool hours' arrangement of 2023` FALSE

@ref akn:art_70__para_a/p10
GIVEN `the arrangements' daily hours` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the hours they offset` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the daily sum of 2023's reduction arrangements` `the arrangements' daily hours` `the hours they offset` IS
    sum `the arrangements' daily hours` MINUS `the hours they offset`

-- (ב): one entitled to the agreed shortening and to fewer hours for one of
-- these has both: (1) a parent's hour off a day, to a year from the birth,
-- by §7(ג)(3) of the Women's Employment Law or Takshir 31.152 or a
-- parallel; (2) absence while the spouse is on reserve duty, by its
-- §7(ג)(6); (3) a moved workplace's temporary approval that hours not
-- worked count; (4) a working parent's shorter day at the end of August by
-- §18 of the framework of 18.4.2016 or a parallel; (5) pool hours, (6)
-- clock rounding, for one employed before the first pulse; (7) travel.
DECLARE `2023 double benefit` IS ONE OF
    `a parent's hour to a year from the birth, 2023`
    `a spouse on reserve duty, 2023`
    `a moved workplace's temporary approval, 2023`
    `the end-of-August parents' day of 2016, kept in 2023`
    `pool hours of one employed before the first pulse, 2023`
    `clock rounding of one employed before the first pulse, 2023`
    `the travel arrangement, kept in 2023`

@ref akn:art_70__para_b akn:art_70__para_b/p2 akn:art_70__para_b__subpara_1 akn:art_70__para_b__subpara_2 akn:art_70__para_b__subpara_3 akn:art_70__para_b__subpara_4 akn:art_70__para_b__subpara_5 akn:art_70__para_b__subpara_6 akn:art_70__para_b__subpara_7
`the benefits §70(ב) of 2023 keeps beside the shortening` MEANS
    LIST `a parent's hour to a year from the birth, 2023`,
         `a spouse on reserve duty, 2023`,
         `a moved workplace's temporary approval, 2023`,
         `the end-of-August parents' day of 2016, kept in 2023`,
         `pool hours of one employed before the first pulse, 2023`,
         `clock rounding of one employed before the first pulse, 2023`,
         `the travel arrangement, kept in 2023`

-- (4) is the 2016 framework's §18 day: ten parents' hours on ten days of
-- the period of use (its `the parents' special leave hours`).
#ASSERT `the parents' special leave hours` EQUALS 10

-- (ג)(1): under the default shortening, one with one or more reduction
-- arrangements uses, beside the day's agreed shortening, the part of the
-- day's reduction that exceeds it — if the day's sum exceeds it (annex ז'
-- gives the computation). (3): never both for the same time.
@ref akn:art_70__para_c akn:art_70__para_c__subpara_1 akn:art_70__para_c__subpara_1/p2 akn:art_70__para_c__subpara_1/p3 akn:art_70__para_c__subpara_3
GIVEN `the day's reduction arrangements` IS A NUMBER, `the day's agreed shortening` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the reduction used beside the 2023 shortening` `the day's reduction arrangements` `the day's agreed shortening` IS
    `not below zero` (`the day's reduction arrangements` MINUS `the day's agreed shortening`)

-- (ג)(2): under a shortening other than the default, (א) one with a
-- reduction arrangement may end his day when he would have without the
-- shortening, completing the week's hours on other days of that week (or
-- another week, with the employer's approval); (ב) he may be short up to
-- the week's reductions less the week's agreed shortening without it
-- counting as missing hours (beyond, it does) — save the holidays'
-- arrangement, (ג) which follows (ג)(1) here too.
@ref akn:art_70__para_c__subpara_2 akn:art_70__para_c__subpara_2__cls_a akn:art_70__para_c__subpara_2__cls_b akn:art_70__para_c__subpara_2__cls_c
GIVEN `the week's reduction arrangements` IS A NUMBER, `the week's agreed shortening` IS A NUMBER, `hours short in the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the missing hours under a 2023 alternative shortening` `the week's reduction arrangements` `the week's agreed shortening` `hours short in the week` IS
    `not below zero` (`hours short in the week` MINUS `not below zero` (`the week's reduction arrangements` MINUS `the week's agreed shortening`))

#ASSERT `the missing hours under a 2023 alternative shortening` 2.5 1.25 1.25 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the missing hours under a 2023 alternative shortening` 2.5 1.25 2 EQUALS 0.75

-- (ד): one whose employment begins with the first pulse or later has clock
-- rounding and pool hours (1) so: (א) if his daily reductions are at least
-- the day's agreed shortening, all of them beside it; (ב) if they are less
-- (or none) and with his clock rounding reach it, pool hours in full and
-- clock rounding of Y = (A + B) − C beside the shortening, if Y > 0; (ג)
-- otherwise, if his reductions save the holidays' and his clock rounding
-- fall short of it, a monthly pool-hours quota of X = D − (C − [A + B]) · E,
-- if X > 0 — A his daily reductions, B his daily clock rounding, C his
-- daily agreed shortening, D his monthly quota but for this, E 21.665 at a
-- five-day week and 26 at a six-day one. (2): (א) the rules of clock
-- rounding and pool hours change only in length; (ב) time worked in them is
-- work time; (ג) this adds to (ג); (ד) A, B, C, D are in parts of an hour,
-- half an hour 0.5.
@desc A new employee's daily and monthly hours, as §70(ד) reads them.
DECLARE `2023 new employee's hours` HAS
    `A, his daily reductions` IS A NUMBER
    `B, his daily clock rounding` IS A NUMBER
    `C, his daily agreed shortening` IS A NUMBER
    `D, his monthly pool quota` IS A NUMBER
    `works a five-day week` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `2023 new employee's rounding and pool` HAS
    `the clock rounding he keeps, a day` IS A NUMBER
    `the pool hours he keeps, a month` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_70__para_d akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_1 akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_1__cls_a akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_1__cls_b akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_1__cls_b__pnt_1 akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_1__cls_b__pnt_2 akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_1__cls_b/p2 akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_1__cls_b/p3 akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_1__cls_b/p4 akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_1__cls_b/p5 akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_1__cls_b/p6 akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_1__cls_c akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_1__cls_c/p2 akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_1__cls_c/p3 akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_1__cls_c/p4 akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_1__cls_c/p5 akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_1__cls_c/p6 akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_1__cls_c/p7 akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_2__cls_d
GIVEN h IS A `2023 new employee's hours`
GIVETH A `2023 new employee's rounding and pool`
DECIDE `what a new employee keeps beside the 2023 shortening` h IS
    IF `the A` AT LEAST `the C`
    THEN `2023 new employee's rounding and pool` `the B` `the D`
    ELSE IF `the A` PLUS `the B` AT LEAST `the C`
         THEN `2023 new employee's rounding and pool` (`not below zero` ((`the A` PLUS `the B`) MINUS `the C`)) `the D`
         ELSE `2023 new employee's rounding and pool` 0 (`not below zero` (`the D` MINUS (`the C` MINUS (`the A` PLUS `the B`)) TIMES `the E`))
    WHERE
        `the A` MEANS h's `A, his daily reductions`
        `the B` MEANS h's `B, his daily clock rounding`
        `the C` MEANS h's `C, his daily agreed shortening`
        `the D` MEANS h's `D, his monthly pool quota`
        `the E` MEANS IF h's `works a five-day week` THEN 21.665 ELSE 26

#ASSERT `what a new employee keeps beside the 2023 shortening` (`2023 new employee's hours` 0.5 0.25 0.25 10 TRUE) EQUALS `2023 new employee's rounding and pool` 0.25 10
#ASSERT `what a new employee keeps beside the 2023 shortening` (`2023 new employee's hours` 0.1 0.25 0.25 10 TRUE) EQUALS `2023 new employee's rounding and pool` 0.1 10
#ASSERT `what a new employee keeps beside the 2023 shortening` (`2023 new employee's hours` 0 0.1 0.5 10 TRUE) EQUALS `2023 new employee's rounding and pool` 0 (10 MINUS 0.4 TIMES 21.665)

@ref akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_2 akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_2__cls_a akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_2__cls_b akn:art_70__para_d__subpara_2__cls_c
`§70(ד) of 2023 changes clock rounding or pool hours beyond their length` MEANS FALSE
`time worked in clock rounding or pool hours is work time under 2023` MEANS TRUE

-- §71: where accumulated rights (annual or monthly quotas, use, balance,
-- redemption at the end) such as rest or sick days are computed in hours,
-- they are adjusted at each pulse to the rate hours were reduced.
@ref akn:art_71/p1
GIVEN `a right in hours` IS A NUMBER, `the week before` IS A NUMBER, `the week after` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a right in hours adjusted to the 2023 shortening` `a right in hours` `the week before` `the week after` IS
    `a right in hours` TIMES `the week after` DIVIDED BY `the week before`

#ASSERT `a right in hours adjusted to the 2023 shortening` 210 42 40 EQUALS 200

-- §72: "עו"ס בטיפול ישיר" — a social worker, full or part time, half of
-- whose hours at least go to treating clients, as the agreement on social
-- workers of 12.12.1976 defines; ¶2 quotes its §19(א): six days a week, 39
-- hours of them as the employer sets, the rest for professional reading
-- and self-study outside the workplace. ¶3: his shortened days are the days
-- he chooses for reading and study, and the time the agreement takes off
-- comes from those hours, not from direct treatment.
@ref akn:art_72/p1 akn:art_72/p2 akn:art_72/p3
`the hours a direct-care social worker gives to treatment each week` MEANS 39

GIVEN `reading hours on the eve` IS A NUMBER, `hours the shortening takes off` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a direct-care social worker's treatment hours after the 2023 shortening` `reading hours on the eve` `hours the shortening takes off` IS
    `the hours a direct-care social worker gives to treatment each week`

-- §73: the parties, joining employers too, cooperate in giving information
-- for an accompanying study of the shortening's effect on pay, hours,
-- overtime, staff and productivity, submitted to a steering committee of
-- the Treasury's wages division, the Histadrut and others agreed.
@ref akn:art_73/p1
`giving information for the study of the shorter week` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `give information for the study of the shorter week`

-- §74: for those the sub-chapter does not reach it is no ground to claim
-- raises, fewer hours or other terms. §75: sub-chapter יד(1) prevails over
-- every other provision, of an agreement or an arrangement, collective or
-- personal, without taking from what it says.
@ref akn:art_74/p1
`the shorter week of 2023 is a ground for those it does not reach` MEANS FALSE

@ref akn:art_75
`sub-chapter יד(1) of 2023 prevails over every other provision` MEANS TRUE

§§ `יד(2) שינויים להגברת היעילות (76–79)`

-- akn:art_76 The heading of §76: role definitions and tasks.
-- akn:art_77 The heading of §77: moving an employee whose role is redundant.
-- akn:art_77__para_h/p2 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.
-- akn:art_78 The heading of §78: new technologies.
-- akn:art_79/p3 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.

-- §76: the Histadrut says it supports adjusting and updating role
-- definitions, tasks added or removed, by the work's needs, and that it and
-- the employees will cooperate; the Histadrut and the employees keep their
-- rights where employees are affected, and each party its steps; declaring
-- a dispute or measures on it needs the Histadrut chairman's approval, and
-- the trade-union division's chairman accompanies its resolution.
@ref akn:art_76/p1
`cooperating with changes to role definitions` MEANS
    PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
    MUST  `cooperate with changes to role definitions`

GIVEN `the Histadrut chairman approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a dispute over role definitions may be declared under 2023` `the Histadrut chairman approved` IF
    `the Histadrut chairman approved`

-- §77: (א) where a role becomes permanently redundant or its activity falls
-- significantly, the Histadrut agrees to the individual move of the
-- employee to another role the employer thinks possible and fit; (ב) by his
-- education and skills, in similar work, keeping the grade span and the
-- level of the post, within the same municipal area; (ג) no substitute post
-- is created soon after; (ד) the employer's rules of keeping pay apply; (ה)
-- the employee takes the training the move needs, at the employer's cost;
-- (ו) where the employer's own rules on moving apply, any consent they ask
-- of the employee, the committee or the Histadrut is deemed given, without
-- taking from the employer's duties by law; (ז) individual moves only; (ח)
-- the trade-union division's chairman takes an unreasonable or abusive use
-- to the follow-up committee.
@desc A move under §77, as far as its terms ask.
DECLARE `2023 move` HAS
    `the role became redundant or fell significantly, for good` IS A BOOLEAN
    `fits his education and skills, in similar work` IS A BOOLEAN
    `keeps the grade span and the post's level` IS A BOOLEAN
    `within the same municipal area` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an individual move` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:art_77__para_a akn:art_77__para_b akn:art_77__para_g
GIVEN m IS A `2023 move`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a move the Histadrut agrees to under 2023` m IF
        m's `the role became redundant or fell significantly, for good`
    AND m's `fits his education and skills, in similar work`
    AND m's `keeps the grade span and the post's level`
    AND m's `within the same municipal area`
    AND m's `an individual move`

#ASSERT NOT `a move the Histadrut agrees to under 2023` (`2023 move` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)

@ref akn:art_77__para_c
`creating a substitute post after a redundancy` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    SHANT `create a substitute post close to a redundancy`

@ref akn:art_77__para_d
`a move under §77 of 2023 keeps pay by the employer's rules` MEANS TRUE

@ref akn:art_77__para_e
`the training a move needs is at the employer's cost` MEANS TRUE

@ref akn:art_77__para_f
GIVEN `the employer's moving rules ask a consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consent to a 2023 move is deemed given` `the employer's moving rules ask a consent` IF
    TRUE

@ref akn:art_77__para_h
`an abuse of §77 of 2023 goes to the follow-up committee` MEANS TRUE

-- §78 (א): the Histadrut supports new technologies and the changes the
-- employers ask in developing, bringing in or embedding them ("שינוי בעניין
-- טכנולוגי"); ¶2: the employer brings its main points to the Histadrut from
-- the early stages, updates it, hears it and weighs its remarks; ¶3: the
-- Histadrut and the employees help and cooperate. (ב): where the change
-- involves none of (1) outsourcing, (2) dismissals, (3) harm to the terms
-- of employment, no dispute is declared and no measure that delays it
-- taken; ¶3: otherwise each party keeps its claims. (ג): declaring a dispute
-- over it needs the approval of the Histadrut's coordination and execution
-- committee, and the trade-union division's chairman accompanies its
-- resolution. (ד): this takes the place of the collective agreement on
-- technologies of 10.1.2018 for the employers that signed it (the corpus
-- holds it; it is not encoded).
@ref akn:art_78__para_a akn:art_78__para_a/p2 akn:art_78__para_a/p3
`bringing a technological change to the Histadrut` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `bring a technological change to the Histadrut's knowledge`

@desc A technological change, as far as §78(ב) asks.
DECLARE `2023 technological change` HAS
    `involves outsourcing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `involves dismissals` IS A BOOLEAN
    `harms the terms of employment` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:art_78__para_b akn:art_78__para_b__subpara_1 akn:art_78__para_b__subpara_2 akn:art_78__para_b__subpara_3 akn:art_78__para_b/p2 akn:art_78__para_b/p3
GIVEN t IS A `2023 technological change`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 2023 technological change is free of disputes` t IF
    NOT (t's `involves outsourcing` OR t's `involves dismissals` OR t's `harms the terms of employment`)

`no dispute that delays a new technology` MEANS
    PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
    SHANT `declare a dispute or take measures that delay a new technology`

@ref akn:art_78__para_c
GIVEN `the coordination and execution committee approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a dispute over a 2023 technological change may be declared` `the coordination and execution committee approved` IF
    `the coordination and execution committee approved`

@ref akn:art_78__para_d
`§78 of 2023 takes the place of the technologies agreement of 10.1.2018` MEANS TRUE

-- §79: sub-chapter יד(2) adds tools and takes none; an employer with other
-- arrangements on its matters may choose, for each of §§76, 77 and 78,
-- them or its own, within 3 months of signing or joining; absent a choice
-- §§76–78 apply. ¶2: the choice is by written notice to the trade-union
-- division's chairman and the wages commissioner.
@ref akn:art_79 akn:art_79/p2
GIVEN `has arrangements of its own` IS A BOOLEAN, `chose its own in writing within 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§§76–78 of 2023 apply at the employer` `has arrangements of its own` `chose its own in writing within 3 months` IF
    NOT (`has arrangements of its own` AND `chose its own in writing within 3 months`)

`choosing between the flexibility measures` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MAY   `choose between the 2023 flexibility measures and the employer's own`

§§ `טו הארכת החופשה המרוכזת באופן חד פעמי (80–81)`

-- akn:chp_15 The heading of chapter טו.

-- §80: where a concentrated leave is customary at Passover 5783, it is
-- lengthened once to take in 13.4.2023 ("יום החופשה הנוסף בחופשה
-- המרוכזת"), as the wages commissioner's circular 2023-1-13 of 23.3.2023
-- set out.
@ref akn:art_80
`the extra day of the Passover leave of 5783` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 13 4 2023

-- §81: an employer that joins by an accession letter, with a concentrated
-- Passover leave in 5783 that it did not lengthen: (א) where it has a
-- concentrated leave at Sukkot or Passover 5784, one of them, as it
-- decides, is lengthened once to take in 28.9.2023 or 21.4.24 ("יום החופשה
-- החליפי למצטרפים"); (ב) the day is taken from the employee's leave balance
-- half on his account and half on the employer's, unless an arrangement
-- lawfully approved there deducts it more favourably to him, which then
-- governs; (ג) the employer's approved rules on the concentrated leave do
-- not change, and the day is treated as the intermediate days of the
-- festival in it, save the deduction; (ד) the employees are told 14 days
-- ahead; (ה) (א) does not apply where the management thinks the leave
-- cannot be lengthened because the public must be served and its
-- director-general told the wages commissioner so, as soon as may be and
-- by 14.9.2023 at the latest, to discuss another answer, (ו) which the
-- follow-up committee discusses.
@ref akn:art_81 akn:art_81__para_a
GIVEN `at Sukkot` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the alternative day for joiners of 2023` `at Sukkot` IS
    IF `at Sukkot` THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 28 9 2023 ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY 21 4 2024

@ref akn:art_81__para_b
GIVEN `the deduction an approved arrangement makes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the part of the alternative day taken from the employee's balance` `the deduction an approved arrangement makes` IS
    min (50%) `the deduction an approved arrangement makes`

#ASSERT `the part of the alternative day taken from the employee's balance` (100%) EQUALS 50%
#ASSERT `the part of the alternative day taken from the employee's balance` 0 EQUALS 0

@ref akn:art_81__para_c
`the alternative day is treated as an intermediate day of the festival` MEANS TRUE

@ref akn:art_81__para_d
`notifying the alternative day` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `notify the alternative leave day 14 days ahead`

@ref akn:art_81__para_e
`the last day to say the leave cannot be lengthened` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 14 9 2023

GIVEN `the management thinks it cannot` IS A BOOLEAN, `told the wages commissioner on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§81(א) of 2023 lengthens the leave` `the management thinks it cannot` `told the wages commissioner on` IF
    NOT (`the management thinks it cannot` AND `told the wages commissioner on` `is on or before` `the last day to say the leave cannot be lengthened`)

@ref akn:art_81__para_f
`another answer for a workplace that cannot lengthen goes to the follow-up committee` MEANS TRUE

§§ `טז–יז הסכם שלוב והסכמים קודמים (82–83)`

-- akn:chp_16 The heading of chapter טז.
-- akn:chp_17 The heading of chapter יז.
-- akn:art_82/p4 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.

-- §82: the agreement is one whole, complete and exhaustive on what it
-- settles, its provisions bound together: none applies without all the
-- others, and sub-chapter יד(1) (the shorter week) does not apply unless
-- יד(2) (flexibility) does. ¶2: an employer that chose its own arrangements
-- under §79 is deemed to apply יד(2). ¶3: this takes nothing from the
-- accession letters, and who may sign them.
@ref akn:art_82 akn:art_82/p2 akn:art_82/p3
GIVEN `sub-chapter יד(2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `chose its own arrangements under §79` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sub-chapter יד(1) of 2023 applies` `sub-chapter יד(2) applies` `chose its own arrangements under §79` IF
    `sub-chapter יד(2) applies` OR `chose its own arrangements under §79`

#ASSERT `sub-chapter יד(1) of 2023 applies` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `sub-chapter יד(1) of 2023 applies` FALSE FALSE

-- §83: the terms set before between the parties, in collective agreements
-- or arrangements or written undertakings, stay in force in the
-- agreement's period, unless one of its provisions amended or cancelled
-- them, expressly or by implication.
@ref akn:art_83
GIVEN `amended or cancelled by this agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an earlier term stays in force under the 2023 framework` `amended or cancelled by this agreement` IF
    NOT `amended or cancelled by this agreement`

§§ `יח תיקון סעיף 19 להסכם המסגרת מיום 18.4.2016 (84–89)`

-- akn:chp_18 The heading of chapter יח.
-- akn:art_88/p2 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.

-- §84: further to §19 of the framework of 18.4.2016 "as amended by the
-- collective agreements of 8.8.2016 and of 11.1.2018" ("הסכם מסגרת 2016"),
-- the Treasury says it means the memorandum of the bill amending the
-- Pensions Law under §19, and the provisions under it, to include: (א) the
-- payments due under it to an eligible retiree or one of the land
-- authority's, or their survivors, for the rise of the determining salary
-- or the pension recomputed ("תשלומים המגיעים לפי סעיף 19 להסכם מסגרת
-- 2016"), for 1.1.2020–31.12.2023, are paid with the pension for January
-- 2025; (ב) linked to the consumer price index from the pension for January
-- 2024 to the pension for January 2025, or to the day the provisions under
-- the amendment set, whichever is later; (ג) those for 1.1.2013–31.12.2019
-- paid after the pension for January 2024, because the right was not yet
-- anchored in legislation (subsidiary legislation among it) that month, are
-- linked from the pension for January 2024 to the day it is; (ד) all of
-- which is beside the Pensions Law's linkage of the determining salary,
-- §19's update among it.
--
-- F-framework-2023-d: the corpus holds the 2016 framework's amendments of
-- 8.8.2016 and of 9.1.2018 ("הכנסת שינויים בהסכם 2016 המתוקן"), and no
-- agreement of 11.1.2018; read as the amendment of 9.1.2018 (convention
-- instruments.cited-instrument-misdated, a pick for the lawyer, MMS-598).
@ref akn:art_84
`the 2016 framework's amendment §84 dates` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 11 1 2018
`the 2016 framework's amendment the corpus holds from January 2018` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 9 1 2018

`§84 dates an amendment of the 2016 framework the corpus holds on another day` MEANS
    NOT (`the 2016 framework's amendment §84 dates` EQUALS `the 2016 framework's amendment the corpus holds from January 2018`)

#ASSERT `§84 dates an amendment of the 2016 framework the corpus holds on another day`

`circulating the 2023 pensions bill` MEANS
    PARTY `the Treasury`
    MUST  `circulate the bill amending the Pensions Law under the 2023 framework`

@ref akn:art_84__para_a
`the period of §19's payments paid in January 2025 opens on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020
`the period of §19's payments paid in January 2025 ends on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2023
`the pension month §19's payments of 2020–2023 are paid with` MEANS `the 2023 framework's month` 2025 1

-- (ב) and (ג): a payment is linked to the index from the pension of
-- January 2024 to the later of its own day and the pension of January 2025
-- (or, for 2013–2019, the day the right is anchored).
@ref akn:art_84__para_b akn:art_84__para_c
GIVEN `the payment` IS A NUMBER, `the index of January 2024's pension` IS A NUMBER, `the index on the day it is paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a §19 payment of 2016 linked under the 2023 framework` `the payment` `the index of January 2024's pension` `the index on the day it is paid` IS
    `the payment` TIMES `the index on the day it is paid` DIVIDED BY `the index of January 2024's pension`

#ASSERT `a §19 payment of 2016 linked under the 2023 framework` 1000 100 103 EQUALS 1030

GIVEN `the day the provisions set` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the pension month §84(ב) links to` `the day the provisions set` IS
    max (`the 2023 framework's month` 2025 1) `the day the provisions set`

@ref akn:art_84__para_d
`§84's linkage is beside the Pensions Law's` MEANS TRUE

-- §85: the Histadrut says §19.2 of the 2016 framework (its undertakings)
-- applies to §84 too. §86: §§19.3 and 19.4, on employers other than the
-- State, apply to it too. §87: notwithstanding 19.4 and §86, an employer
-- 19.4 reaches may, with the wages commissioner's approval of how, apply
-- 19.4 before the State applies the rise to its own pensioners. §88: and if
-- in January 2024 the right under §19 is not yet anchored in legislation,
-- the wages commissioner does not object to the employers below, whom 19.3
-- reaches, applying it before the State, with his approval of how: ¶3–¶4,
-- the Centre of Local Government, the three large cities, the Centre of
-- Regional Councils and the Union of Religious Councils.
@ref akn:art_85 akn:art_86
`§§19.2–19.4 of the 2016 framework reach §84 of 2023` MEANS TRUE

@ref akn:art_87
GIVEN `the wages commissioner approved how` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a §19.4 employer may go before the State under 2023` `the wages commissioner approved how` IF
    `the wages commissioner approved how`

@ref akn:art_88 akn:art_88/p3 akn:art_88/p4
`the employers §88 of 2023 names` MEANS
    LIST "מרכז השלטון המקומי", "שלוש הערים הגדולות", "מרכז המועצות האזוריות", "חבר המועצות הדתיות"

GIVEN `anchored in legislation by January 2024` IS A BOOLEAN, `the wages commissioner approved how` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a §19.3 employer may go before the State under 2023` `anchored in legislation by January 2024` `the wages commissioner approved how` IF
    (NOT `anchored in legislation by January 2024`) AND `the wages commissioner approved how`

-- Every employer §88 names is one §19.3 of 2016 reaches.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD elem n `the signatories §19.3 of 2016 reaches`) `the employers §88 of 2023 names`

-- §89: §84(ב) and (ג)'s linkage applies too to the payments for the rise of
-- the jubilee grant under §19.5 of the 2016 framework that meet them.
@ref akn:art_89
`§84's linkage reaches the jubilee grant of §19.5` MEANS TRUE

§§ `יט גמלאים בפנסיה תקציבית (90–96)`

-- akn:chp_19 The heading of chapter יט.
-- akn:art_90__para_b/p14 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.
-- akn:art_90__para_e/p4 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.
-- akn:art_90__para_g/p9 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.
-- akn:art_91 The heading of §91: the Histadrut says.
-- akn:art_91__para_b/p2 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.
-- akn:art_96/p2 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.

-- §90: the Treasury says it means to circulate the memorandum of a bill
-- amending the State Service (Pensions) Law ("חוק הגמלאות") on these
-- principles. (א): it reaches one who retired under the law from 1 January
-- 2020 to 31 March 2027 and whose scale on the eve of retiring is in annex
-- ח1' ("פורש זכאי").
@ref akn:art_90 akn:art_90__para_a
`the 2023 pensioners' window opens on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020
`the 2023 pensioners' window ends on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2027

GIVEN `retired on` IS A DATE, `scale on the eve` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an eligible retiree under the 2023 framework` `retired on` `scale on the eve` IF
        `retired on` `is on or after` `the 2023 pensioners' window opens on`
    AND `retired on` `is on or before` `the 2023 pensioners' window ends on`
    AND elem `scale on the eve` `the scales of annex ח1'`

#ASSERT `an eligible retiree under the 2023 framework` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2027) "מינהלי"
#ASSERT NOT `an eligible retiree under the 2023 framework` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2027) "מינהלי"

-- (ב): the determining salary is raised, for an eligible retiree or his
-- survivors, by S = Y + Z: Y = X · 500 − A, taken as 0 if negative; Z = 0 to
-- 30.11.2024 and from 1.12.2024 (X · 5% − B) · C − M, taken as 0 if
-- negative; M = A − X · 500, taken as 0 if negative. X the coefficient of
-- annex ח2' by the month he retired; A the 2023 shekel supplement he had on
-- the eve of retiring; B the 2024 percentage supplement's rate he had then;
-- C his determining salary by the Pensions Law, without (א) the
-- recuperation and clothing allowances, (ב) supplements not updated by the
-- cost-of-living agreements that have another mechanism, (ג) the
-- minimum-wage top-up, (ד) supplements first paid after 31.12.2022, this
-- agreement's or one under §50 among them (a named input).
@ref akn:art_90__para_b akn:art_90__para_b/p2 akn:art_90__para_b/p3 akn:art_90__para_b/p4 akn:art_90__para_b/p5 akn:art_90__para_b/p6 akn:art_90__para_b/p16 akn:art_90__para_b/p17 akn:art_90__para_b/p18
GIVEN X IS A NUMBER, `the A` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Y of the 2023 pensioners` X `the A` IS
    `not below zero` (X TIMES 500 MINUS `the A`)

GIVEN X IS A NUMBER, `the A` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `M of the 2023 pensioners` X `the A` IS
    `not below zero` (`the A` MINUS X TIMES 500)

@ref akn:art_90__para_b/p7 akn:art_90__para_b/p8 akn:art_90__para_b/p9 akn:art_90__para_b/p10 akn:art_90__para_b/p11 akn:art_90__para_b/p12 akn:art_90__para_b/p13 akn:art_90__para_b/p15 akn:art_90__para_b__subpara_a akn:art_90__para_b__subpara_b akn:art_90__para_b__subpara_c akn:art_90__para_b__subpara_d
`Z of the 2023 pensioners starts on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2024

GIVEN d IS A DATE, X IS A NUMBER, `the A` IS A NUMBER, `the B` IS A NUMBER, `the C` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Z of the 2023 pensioners on` d X `the A` `the B` `the C` IS
    IF d `is on or after` `Z of the 2023 pensioners starts on`
    THEN `not below zero` ((X TIMES 5% MINUS `the B`) TIMES `the C` MINUS `M of the 2023 pensioners` X `the A`)
    ELSE 0

GIVEN d IS A DATE, X IS A NUMBER, `the A` IS A NUMBER, `the B` IS A NUMBER, `the C` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `S of the 2023 pensioners on` d X `the A` `the B` `the C` IS
    `Y of the 2023 pensioners` X `the A` PLUS `Z of the 2023 pensioners on` d X `the A` `the B` `the C`

-- One who retired in 12.2022 (X = 37.5%), with no 2023 supplement and no
-- 2024 rate on the eve, a C of 10,000: Y = 187.5; Z = 187.5 from 1.12.2024.
#ASSERT `S of the 2023 pensioners on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2024) (37.5%) 0 0 10000 EQUALS 187.5
#ASSERT `S of the 2023 pensioners on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2024) (37.5%) 0 0 10000 EQUALS 375
-- One who had 400 on the eve (X = 59.38%): Y = 0, M = 103.1, and Z is cut by M.
#ASSERT `Y of the 2023 pensioners` (59.38%) 400 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `M of the 2023 pensioners` (59.38%) 400 EQUALS 103.1

-- (ג): where an employee of the grade the retiree had on the eve (§8 of the
-- Pensions Law) has the 2024 percentage supplement raised by 1% by §38's
-- default, from 1.4.2027 Z = (X · 5% − B) · C + X · 1% · C − M, taken as 0
-- if negative, in place of (ב)'s. (ד): where a scale of annex ח1' did not
-- have that 1%, the follow-up committee discusses how §90 applies to the
-- last pulse for its retirees.
@ref akn:art_90__para_c akn:art_90__para_c/p2 akn:art_90__para_c/p3
GIVEN d IS A DATE, X IS A NUMBER, `the A` IS A NUMBER, `the B` IS A NUMBER, `the C` IS A NUMBER, `the grade had §38's 1%` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Z of the 2023 pensioners with §38 on` d X `the A` `the B` `the C` `the grade had §38's 1%` IS
    IF `the grade had §38's 1%` AND d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2027)
    THEN `not below zero` ((X TIMES 5% MINUS `the B`) TIMES `the C` PLUS X TIMES 1% TIMES `the C` MINUS `M of the 2023 pensioners` X `the A`)
    ELSE `Z of the 2023 pensioners on` d X `the A` `the B` `the C`

#ASSERT `Z of the 2023 pensioners with §38 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2027) (50%) 0 0 10000 TRUE EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `Z of the 2023 pensioners with §38 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2027) (50%) 0 0 10000 FALSE EQUALS 250

@ref akn:art_90__para_d
`the last pulse of a scale without §38's 1% goes to the follow-up committee` MEANS TRUE

-- (ה): it reaches too one who retired in that window from the border
-- crossings' scale ("פורש זכאי בדירוג מעברי הגבול"), for whom, in place of
-- (א)–(ד), S = X · G − A, taken as 0 if negative: X the coefficient of annex
-- ח3' by his month; G the whole shekel sum this agreement raised the basic
-- salary of his grade by, and A the sum it had raised his own by on the eve
-- of retiring, both from the table of annex ח3'.
@ref akn:art_90__para_e akn:art_90__para_e/p2 akn:art_90__para_e/p3 akn:art_90__para_e/p5 akn:art_90__para_e/p6 akn:art_90__para_e/p7 akn:art_90__para_e/p8 akn:art_90__para_e/p9
GIVEN X IS A NUMBER, G IS A NUMBER, `the A` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `S of a 2023 border-crossings pensioner` X G `the A` IS
    `not below zero` (X TIMES G MINUS `the A`)

#ASSERT `S of a 2023 border-crossings pensioner` (50%) 822.43 0 EQUALS 411.215
#ASSERT `S of a 2023 border-crossings pensioner` (50%) 822.43 500 EQUALS 0

-- (ו): the rise comes gradually, by the month he retired and the pulses of
-- annexes ח2' and ח3'.
@ref akn:art_90__para_f
`the 2023 pensioners' rise is gradual by annexes ח2' and ח3'` MEANS TRUE

-- (ז): it reaches too one who retired in that window from the Israel Land
-- Authority's scale ("פורש זכאי בדירוג רשות מקרקעי ישראל"), in place of
-- (א)–(ו): for him or his survivors, where but for chapter ג'2 of the
-- Pensions Law "the salary on the eve of retiring" would exceed "the salary
-- ceiling" (its §§63יד and 63יג), the pension is recomputed, as annex ח4''s
-- table dates, as if the ceiling were higher by S = Y + Z: Y = X · 500 − A,
-- 0 if negative; Z = 0 "in the period to 30.11.2024", and (X · 6% − B) · C −
-- M "in the period from 1.1.2024"; M = A − X · 500, 0 if negative. X by
-- annex ח4'; A the 2023 shekel supplement he had on the eve; B the rate his
-- basic salary had been raised from "the authority's salary base" by annex
-- ו' on the eve, as annex ח4' sets out; C his basic salary for the month he
-- retired or for November 2024, whichever is earlier, with the in-service
-- training allowances א' and ב' and the management allowance he had for it.
-- ¶19: S comes in stages by his month and annex ח4''s pulses.
--
-- F-framework-2023-b: the two periods of Z overlap, 1.1.2024–30.11.2024,
-- where (ב) starts its Z on 1.12.2024, annex ו' raises the land authority's
-- salaries by percentage from 1.12.2024, and annex ח4''s pulse 3 is 12/24;
-- read 1.12.2024 (convention reading.misprint).
-- F-framework-2023-c: (ז) says nothing of a negative Z, where (ב) and (ג)
-- take it as 0; it is taken as 0 (convention amounts.never-negative).
@ref akn:art_90__para_g akn:art_90__para_g/p2 akn:art_90__para_g/p3 akn:art_90__para_g/p4 akn:art_90__para_g/p5 akn:art_90__para_g/p6 akn:art_90__para_g/p7 akn:art_90__para_g/p8 akn:art_90__para_g/p10 akn:art_90__para_g/p11 akn:art_90__para_g/p12 akn:art_90__para_g/p13 akn:art_90__para_g/p14 akn:art_90__para_g/p15 akn:art_90__para_g/p16 akn:art_90__para_g/p17 akn:art_90__para_g/p18 akn:art_90__para_g/p19
`the end of (ז)'s first period of Z` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 11 2024
`the start (ז) prints for its second period of Z` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2024
`the start of (ז)'s second period of Z, as read` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2024

`§90(ז)'s two periods of Z overlap` MEANS
        DATE_SERIAL `the start (ז) prints for its second period of Z` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the end of (ז)'s first period of Z`
    AND `the start of (ז)'s second period of Z, as read` EQUALS `Z of the 2023 pensioners starts on`

#ASSERT `§90(ז)'s two periods of Z overlap`

`§90(ז) prints no floor for Z where (ב) and (ג) do` MEANS TRUE
#ASSERT `§90(ז) prints no floor for Z where (ב) and (ג) do`

GIVEN `retired on` IS A DATE, `in the land authority's scale on the eve` IS A BOOLEAN, `the eve's salary would exceed the ceiling` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an eligible land-authority retiree under the 2023 framework` `retired on` `in the land authority's scale on the eve` `the eve's salary would exceed the ceiling` IF
        `retired on` `is on or after` `the 2023 pensioners' window opens on`
    AND `retired on` `is on or before` `the 2023 pensioners' window ends on`
    AND `in the land authority's scale on the eve`
    AND `the eve's salary would exceed the ceiling`

GIVEN d IS A DATE, X IS A NUMBER, `the A` IS A NUMBER, `the B` IS A NUMBER, `the C` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `S of a 2023 land-authority pensioner on` d X `the A` `the B` `the C` IS
    `Y of the 2023 pensioners` X `the A` PLUS `the Z`
    WHERE
        `the Z` MEANS
            IF d `is on or after` `the start of (ז)'s second period of Z, as read`
            THEN `not below zero` ((X TIMES 6% MINUS `the B`) TIMES `the C` MINUS `M of the 2023 pensioners` X `the A`)
            ELSE 0

#ASSERT `S of a 2023 land-authority pensioner on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2024) (50%) 0 0 10000 EQUALS 250
#ASSERT `S of a 2023 land-authority pensioner on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2024) (50%) 0 0 10000 EQUALS 550
#ASSERT `S of a 2023 land-authority pensioner on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2024) (10%) 500 (2%) 10000 EQUALS 0

-- §91: the Histadrut says (א) the amendment's principles are acceptable to
-- it and it will support the legislation; (ב) once the Knesset passes it,
-- it will make no demand to raise the determining salary, or for another
-- supplement or benefit, for the costs or benefits agreed here or in the
-- agreements signed alongside, or under them, or in any agreement, for the
-- time to 31.12.2027.
@ref akn:art_91__para_a
`supporting the 2023 pensions bill` MEANS
    PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
    MUST  `support the bill amending the Pensions Law under the 2023 framework`

@ref akn:art_91__para_b
GIVEN `the Knesset passed the amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Histadrut may demand more for the 2023 pensioners` `the Knesset passed the amendment` IF
    NOT `the Knesset passed the amendment`

`no further demand for the 2023 pensioners` MEANS
    PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
    SHANT `demand a further rise of the determining salary for the 2023 frame`

-- §92: the amendment applies by the same rules, payment days among them,
-- to every employer or employers' organisation among whom the Pensions Law
-- applies by law, agreement or arrangement; adapted to their scales that
-- annex ח1' includes, and to the scales of neighbourhood and settlement
-- rabbis and of youth, society and community education in the local
-- authorities, and to their other scales the State does not have, with the
-- wages commissioner's approval. ¶2: among the signatories, the Centre of
-- Local Government, the three large cities, the Centre of Regional
-- Councils, "מרכז המועצות הדתיות", the National Insurance Institute and the
-- Employment Service.
@ref akn:art_92 akn:art_92/p2
`the signatories §92 of 2023 names` MEANS
    LIST "מרכז השלטון המקומי", "שלוש הערים הגדולות", "מרכז המועצות האזוריות", "מרכז המועצות הדתיות", "המוסד לביטוח לאומי", "שירות התעסוקה"

GIVEN scale IS A STRING, `in annex ח1'` IS A BOOLEAN, `a scale the State has` IS A BOOLEAN, `the wages commissioner approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2023 pensions amendment reaches a scale of a §92 employer` scale `in annex ח1'` `a scale the State has` `the wages commissioner approved` IF
        `in annex ח1'`
    OR  scale EQUALS "רבני שכונות והתיישבות"
    OR  scale EQUALS "חינוך נוער חברה וקהילה"
    OR  ((NOT `a scale the State has`) AND `the wages commissioner approved`)

#ASSERT `the 2023 pensions amendment reaches a scale of a §92 employer` "חינוך נוער חברה וקהילה" FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- §93: an employer §92 does not reach that has a budgetary pension by
-- agreement or arrangement applies the amendment, adapted, to one who left
-- its service on §90(א)'s terms, with no further terms or demands, subject
-- to the wages commissioner's approval: among the signatories, the Hebrew
-- University and the Technion — those §19.4 of 2016 names.
@ref akn:art_93
`the signatories §93 of 2023 names` MEANS LIST "האוניברסיטה העברית", "הטכניון"

#ASSERT `the signatories §93 of 2023 names` EQUALS `the signatories §19.4 of 2016 reaches`

-- §94: for an eligible retiree entitled to a jubilee grant, or his
-- survivors, the salary the jubilee component is computed on grows by S,
-- gradually as the determining salary does, provided S's supplements count
-- for the hour value; ¶2: for one of the land authority's whose pension is
-- recomputed by §90(ז), the jubilee grant is recomputed too, by annex ח4''s
-- pulses, by the same S; ¶3: "מענק יובל" is Takshir 25.5's and its
-- parallels; ¶4: the day it is paid does not change.
@ref akn:art_94 akn:art_94/p2 akn:art_94/p3
GIVEN S IS A NUMBER, `S's supplements count for the hour value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the jubilee grant base's rise under the 2023 framework` S `S's supplements count for the hour value` IS
    IF `S's supplements count for the hour value` THEN S ELSE 0

@ref akn:art_94/p4
`§94 of 2023 changes when the jubilee component is paid` MEANS FALSE

-- §95: it does not concern employers without a budgetary pension; neither
-- they nor their employees get another benefit, directly or not, for it or
-- its cost, and no claim is made for one. §96: it approves no benefit
-- contrary to §29 of the Budget Foundations Law, in computing the
-- determining salary, the pension or a jubilee grant among it.
@ref akn:art_95
GIVEN `the employer has a budgetary pension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a benefit for §90's cost of 2023` `the employer has a budgetary pension` IF
    FALSE

`no benefit elsewhere for the 2023 pensioners' rise` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    SHANT `give another benefit for the 2023 pensioners' rise`

@ref akn:art_96
`chapter יט of 2023 is an approval under §29` MEANS FALSE

§§ `כ–כד סכסוכים, מיצוי תביעות, שקט תעשייתי, ועדת מעקב ובוררות (97–110)`

-- akn:chp_20 The heading of chapter כ.
-- akn:chp_21 The heading of chapter כא.
-- akn:chp_22 The heading of chapter כב.
-- akn:art_104__para_g/p2 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.
-- akn:chp_23 The heading of chapter כג.
-- akn:chp_24 The heading of chapter כד.

-- §97: the Histadrut says every collective dispute, national or local,
-- declared or notified with the employers party to the agreement (or
-- joining it), is void on the signing, save those annex ט lists.
@ref akn:art_97
GIVEN `the dispute's group` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a dispute stays open after the 2023 framework` `the dispute's group` IF
    elem `the dispute's group` (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the 2023 row's label`) `the open disputes of annex ט`)

#ASSERT `a dispute stays open after the 2023 framework` "עובדים סוציאליים"
#ASSERT NOT `a dispute stays open after the 2023 framework` "אחר"

-- §98: the Histadrut exhausts all its claims on chapter יד for the time to
-- 31.12.2027; §99: and all its claims on pay supplements and terms, or any
-- further benefit, economic claims of any kind, for that time. §100:
-- subject to chapter יב, no further negotiation on wage agreements or
-- benefits, nationally or otherwise, for the employees it covers, save as
-- the problem-solving agreement signed alongside says in writing. §101:
-- this adds to the exhaustion provisions that apply, or will, in the
-- public sector.
@ref akn:art_98 akn:art_99 akn:art_100 akn:art_101
`the 2023 framework's exhaustion of claims runs to` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2027

`no further negotiation on pay to 31.12.2027` MEANS
    PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
    SHANT `negotiate further on pay for the period to 31.12.2027`

-- §102: the Histadrut takes no strike, full or partial, or other harm to
-- the work against any employer or unit over a demand on chapter יד, to
-- 31.12.2027; §103: nor, in the agreement's period, over any demand that
-- costs the public employers or seeks further benefits; §104: save over (א)
-- a demand that costs nothing against what is actually in force (a pay
-- cut, harm to terms, bullying at work); (ב) dismissals; (ג) outsourcing;
-- (ד) organising a workplace for the first time; (ה) the effects of
-- privatising it; (ו) another matter (an employer's, the Government's, the
-- legislature's or a regulator's decision) with a clear, immediate and
-- certain effect, where the trade-union division's chairman approved
-- measures in writing; (ז) a public employer refusing understandings the
-- wages commissioner and the Histadrut accepted in negotiation under
-- §§4(ב) or 4(ג)(1) of the problem-solving agreement, to anchor them; (ח)
-- the structure of employment under §56. ¶2: no party's claims on the
-- merits are taken away. §105: this adds to the industrial-peace provisions
-- that apply, or will.
@ref akn:art_102
`no strike over the 2023 productivity chapter` MEANS
    PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
    SHANT `strike or harm the work over the productivity chapter to 31.12.2027`

DECLARE `2023 industrial-peace matter` IS ONE OF
    `a 2023 demand that costs the public employers`
    `a 2023 demand that costs nothing against what is in force`
    `dismissals under the 2023 framework`
    `outsourcing under the 2023 framework`
    `organising a workplace for the first time under the 2023 framework`
    `the effects of privatising a workplace under the 2023 framework`
    `another decision whose effect the chairman approved measures over in writing, 2023`
    `an employer refusing the problem-solving agreement's understandings, 2023`
    `the structure of employment under §56 of 2023`

@ref akn:art_103 akn:art_104 akn:art_104__para_a akn:art_104__para_b akn:art_104__para_c akn:art_104__para_d akn:art_104__para_e akn:art_104__para_f akn:art_104__para_g akn:art_104__para_h akn:art_104/p2
GIVEN m IS A `2023 industrial-peace matter`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Histadrut may strike under the 2023 framework over` m `on` d IF
    (NOT `in the 2023 framework agreement's period` d) OR NOT (m EQUALS `a 2023 demand that costs the public employers`)

#ASSERT NOT `the Histadrut may strike under the 2023 framework over` `a 2023 demand that costs the public employers` `on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2025)
#ASSERT `the Histadrut may strike under the 2023 framework over` `dismissals under the 2023 framework` `on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2025)

`no strike over a costly demand in the 2023 period` MEANS
    PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
    SHANT `strike or harm the work over a demand that costs the public employers`

@ref akn:art_105
`the 2023 industrial peace adds to the provisions in force` MEANS TRUE

-- §106: a follow-up committee of the wages commissioner and the chairman
-- of the Histadrut's trade-union division goes on following and helping to
-- carry out the agreement and decides the disagreements over it; ¶2: its
-- decisions are final and bind the parties.
@ref akn:art_106 akn:art_106/p2
`deciding disputes over the 2023 framework` MEANS
    PARTY `the follow-up committee`
    MUST  `decide disputes over the 2023 framework agreement`

`the 2023 follow-up committee's decisions are final` MEANS TRUE

-- §107: the agreement on the institution for agreed arbitration in the
-- public services is extended to the signing of the next national wage
-- agreement. §108: an agreement amending it to allow mediation by consent
-- is signed alongside. §109: within 90 days of the signing the State and
-- the Histadrut (א) update its list of members (arbitrators) by agreement,
-- by its §3; (ב) draw up a list of mediators by agreement, for appointing
-- one or more to an agreed mediation under §108's agreement. §110: chapter
-- כד reaches the employers party to the arbitration agreement or joining
-- it by its terms.
@ref akn:art_107 akn:art_108
`the arbitration institution's agreement runs to the next national wage agreement` MEANS TRUE

@ref akn:art_109 akn:art_109__para_a akn:art_109__para_b
`the days to update the arbitrators and list the mediators` MEANS 90

`updating the arbitrators` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `update the list of arbitrators within 90 days`

`listing the mediators` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `draw up a list of mediators within 90 days`

@ref akn:art_110
GIVEN `a party to the arbitration agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `chapter כד of 2023 reaches the employer` `a party to the arbitration agreement` IF
    `a party to the arbitration agreement`

