-- A row of one of annex ו''s tables: its label (a grade, a post, a
-- seniority, a level) and its cells, in the columns' order of days.
@desc A row of one of the framework's annexed tables: its label and its cells.
DECLARE `2023 annex row` HAS
    `the 2023 row's label` IS A STRING
    `the 2023 row's cells` IS A LIST OF NUMBER

-- The rates of the percentage steps, in the annex's columns' order: the
-- 2024 percentage supplement's (§§27, 36–38) — 2%, 3.5%, 5%, 6%.
`the 2023 annex's rates` MEANS
    map (GIVEN s YIELD s's `the 2024 step's rate`) `the steps of the 2024 percentage supplement`

#ASSERT `the 2023 annex's rates` EQUALS LIST 2%, 3.5%, 5%, 6%

-- Each later cell is the row's first raised by its column's rate, to the
-- agora.
GIVEN r IS A `2023 annex row`, rates IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 2023 annex row keeps the rates` r rates IF
    CONSIDER r's `the 2023 row's cells`
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
            count rest EQUALS count rates
        AND all (GIVEN p YIELD (fst p) `is within an agora of` (`to the agora` (first `increased by` (snd p)))) (zip rest rates)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- A range row prints a lower and an upper bound for each day: each pair is
-- the first pair raised by its column's rate, to the agora.
GIVEN r IS A `2023 annex row`, rates IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 2023 range row keeps the rates` r rates IF
    CONSIDER r's `the 2023 row's cells`
    WHEN lo FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (CONSIDER rest
         WHEN hi FOLLOWED BY pairs THEN
                 count pairs EQUALS 2 TIMES count rates
             AND all (GIVEN p YIELD (fst p) `is within an agora of` (snd p))
                     (zip pairs (concat (map (GIVEN k YIELD LIST `to the agora` (lo `increased by` k), `to the agora` (hi `increased by` k)) rates)))
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- A later table is an earlier one raised by a rate, cell for cell, to the
-- agora; rows matched by place and label.
GIVEN later IS A LIST OF `2023 annex row`
      earlier IS A LIST OF `2023 annex row`
      rate IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 2023 table is another raised by` later earlier rate IF
        count later EQUALS count earlier
    AND all (GIVEN p YIELD
                     (fst p)'s `the 2023 row's label` EQUALS (snd p)'s `the 2023 row's label`
                 AND count ((fst p)'s `the 2023 row's cells`) EQUALS count ((snd p)'s `the 2023 row's cells`)
                 AND all (GIVEN c YIELD (fst c) `is within an agora of` (`to the agora` ((snd c) `increased by` rate)))
                         (zip ((fst p)'s `the 2023 row's cells`) ((snd p)'s `the 2023 row's cells`)))
            (zip later earlier)

GIVEN rows IS A LIST OF `2023 annex row`
      label IS A STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the cells of the 2023 row labelled` rows label IS
    foldl (GIVEN acc, r YIELD IF r's `the 2023 row's label` EQUALS label THEN r's `the 2023 row's cells` ELSE acc) EMPTY rows

-- א: the border crossings, in the State's service. ¶2: §15 of the agreement
-- of 2.3.2009 on the scale is carried out so: ¶3–¶4 and the table, the
-- basic salary table is updated on the table's days (to 30.6.2023, from
-- 1.7.2023, 1.10.2024, 1.12.2024, 1.4.2025, 1.4.2026, 1.4.2027). The text
-- states no rule for its cells; what the checks find is that every grade
-- rises by the 2023 shekel supplement — 400 from 1.7.2023 and 100 more
-- from 1.10.2024 — and then by four shekel steps whose base the annex does
-- not print; and that annex ח3''s G and A are this table's rises, to the
-- agora.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__para_a akn:att_6__hc_1__para_a/p2 akn:att_6__hc_1__para_a/p3 akn:att_6__hc_1__para_a/p4 akn:att_6__hc_1__para_a/t1
GIVEN r IS A `2023 annex row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a border-crossings row of 2023 rises by the shekel supplement` r IF
    CONSIDER r's `the 2023 row's cells`
    WHEN c0 FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (CONSIDER rest
         WHEN c1 FOLLOWED BY rest2 THEN
             (CONSIDER rest2
              WHEN c2 FOLLOWED BY more THEN
                      (c1 MINUS c0) `is within an agora of` `the 2023 shekel supplement for a full position`
                  AND (c2 MINUS c1) `is within an agora of` `the 2023 shekel supplement's rise`
                  AND count more EQUALS 4
              OTHERWISE FALSE)
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

#ASSERT all `a border-crossings row of 2023 rises by the shekel supplement` `the border crossings' basic table of 2023`
#ASSERT count `the border crossings' basic table of 2023` EQUALS 13

-- ב: the judges' typists. ¶2: §6.3 of the agreement of 28.12.2009 on the
-- scale ("הסכם הקלדניות") is carried out so: (א) the basic salary table, for
-- a full position, on the table's days; (ב) further to its §8.1, the typing
-- supplement's shekel sum follows level 5 of the basic table, its other
-- rules unchanged; (ג) from 1.7.2023 they have the 2023 shekel supplement by
-- chapter ה's rules, at the table's sums (400, then 500 from 1.10.2024).
-- Every cell is the first column's at the 2024 rates, to the agora.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__para_b akn:att_6__hc_1__para_b/p2 akn:att_6__hc_1__para_b__subpara_a akn:att_6__hc_1__para_b__subpara_a/p2 akn:att_6__hc_1__para_b__subpara_a/t1 akn:att_6__hc_1__para_b__subpara_b akn:att_6__hc_1__para_b__subpara_b/p2 akn:att_6__hc_1__para_b__subpara_b/t1
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD `a 2023 annex row keeps the rates` r `the 2023 annex's rates`) `the judges' typists' basic table of 2023`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD `a 2023 annex row keeps the rates` r `the 2023 annex's rates`) `the typing supplement of 2023`

-- The typing supplement follows level 5: its rise in each column is level
-- 5's, to the agora.
GIVEN s IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      l IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2023 typing supplement follows level 5` s l IF
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN s0 FOLLOWED BY srest THEN
        (CONSIDER l
         WHEN l0 FOLLOWED BY lrest THEN
             all (GIVEN p YIELD (fst p) `is within an agora of` (s0 TIMES (snd p) DIVIDED BY l0)) (zip srest lrest)
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

#ASSERT `the 2023 typing supplement follows level 5` (`the cells of the 2023 row labelled` `the typing supplement of 2023` "") (`the cells of the 2023 row labelled` `the judges' typists' basic table of 2023` "5")

