§§ `נספח ז' — דוגמאות ונוסחאות לסעיף 70(ג)`

-- akn:att_7__hc_1/p1 The annex's title; no rule.
-- akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p23 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.
-- akn:att_7__hc_1/p11 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.

-- (1), under the default (§70(ג)(1)): on a working day one with a reduction
-- arrangement other than clock rounding or pool hours uses, beside the
-- agreed shortening, C = A − B: A the day's sum of reductions but for this
-- agreement, B the day's agreed shortening. C ≤ 0: none; C > 0: the
-- agreement's rules for the shortening and the arrangement's for the rest.
-- Example 1: a working parent's 0.5 hour against the first pulse's 0.25:
-- 0.25 more (7:30–16:00: the parent's rules 15:30–15:45, the agreement's
-- 15:45–16:00). Example 2: 2 hours on the intermediate days against the
-- second pulse's 0.5: 1.5 more (14:00–15:30 the festival's rules,
-- 15:30–16:00 the agreement's).
@ref akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p2 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p3 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p4 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p5 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p6 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p7 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p8 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p9 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p10 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p11 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p12 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p13 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p14 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p15 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p16 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p17 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p18 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p19 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p20 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p21 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1/p22
#ASSERT `the reduction used beside the 2023 shortening` 0.5 (`what a pulse of 2023 takes off a day` 42 41) EQUALS 0.25
#ASSERT `the reduction used beside the 2023 shortening` 2 (2 TIMES `what a pulse of 2023 takes off a day` 42 41) EQUALS 1.5
#ASSERT `the reduction used beside the 2023 shortening` 0.25 0.5 EQUALS 0

-- (2), not the default (§70(ג)(2)): a working parent of 0.5 hours a day,
-- whose workplace worked 7:30–16:00 Sunday to Wednesday and 7:30–15:30 on
-- Thursday before (42 hours), and after the second pulse 7:30–15:00 on
-- Sunday and Tuesday, 7:30–16:00 on Monday and Wednesday and 7:30–15:30 on
-- Thursday (40 hours): he may leave at 15:30 on Monday and Wednesday as on
-- the eve, accruing a shortage he completes in the week; he leaves at
-- 15:00 on Sunday and Tuesday with none, and past the new day of 7.5 hours
-- there is overtime; working to 16:00 on Monday and Wednesday is his
-- ordinary pay. His week's reductions, 2.5 hours, exceed the week's
-- agreed shortening, 2, by 0.5 — the most he may be short (§70(ג)(2)(ב)).
@ref akn:att_7__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_7__hc_1/p2 akn:att_7__hc_1/p3 akn:att_7__hc_1/p4 akn:att_7__hc_1/p5 akn:att_7__hc_1/p6 akn:att_7__hc_1/p7 akn:att_7__hc_1/p8 akn:att_7__hc_1/p9 akn:att_7__hc_1/p10
`the example's week after the second pulse` MEANS 7.5 PLUS 8.5 PLUS 7.5 PLUS 8.5 PLUS 8
`the example's week on the eve` MEANS 4 TIMES 8.5 PLUS 8

#ASSERT `the example's week on the eve` EQUALS 42
#ASSERT `the example's week after the second pulse` EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `the missing hours under a 2023 alternative shortening` (5 TIMES 0.5) (`the example's week on the eve` MINUS `the example's week after the second pulse`) 0.5 EQUALS 0

§§ `נספחים ח1'–ח4' — גמלאים בפנסיה תקציבית`

-- akn:att_8__hc_1/p1 The annex's title: the pensioners' scales (chapter יט); no rule.
-- akn:att_8__hc_1/p2 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.
-- akn:att_9__hc_1/p2 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.
-- akn:att_9__hc_1/p3 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.
-- akn:att_10__hc_1/p1 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.
-- akn:att_11__hc_1/p2 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.
-- akn:att_11__hc_1/p3 Signatures and initials on the page; no rule.

-- ח1': the 24 scales of §90(א) — jurists, public defenders and state
-- attorneys save one whose determining salary was computed by a judicial
-- officer's pay.
@ref akn:att_8__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_3 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_4 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_5 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_6 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_7 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_8 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_9 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_10 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_11 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_12 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_13 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_14 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_15 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_16 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_17 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_18 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_19 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_20 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_21 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_22 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_23 akn:att_8__hc_1__para_24
`the scales of annex ח1'` MEANS
    LIST "מינהלי", "אחיד", "טכנאי רנטגן", "מח\"ר", "מהנדסים", "טכנאים והנדסאים", "פיזיותרפיסטים",
         "משפטנים", "סנגורים ציבוריים", "עיתונאים", "עובדי מעבדה, ביוכימאים ומיקרוביולוגים", "רוקחים",
         "אחים ואחיות", "פארה רפואיים", "מרפאים בעיסוק", "מפקחים ימיים", "מקצ\"ט", "מעברי הגבול",
         "רשות מקרקעי ישראל", "כבאים", "עובדים סוציאליים", "שירות החוץ", "פרקליטים", "קלדניות שופטים"

#ASSERT count `the scales of annex ח1'` EQUALS 24
#ASSERT NOT elem "עובדי הוראה" `the scales of annex ח1'`

-- ח2' (and ח4', for the land authority): for each month of retiring (the
-- last month worked), from 1.2020 to 3.2027, the coefficient X and, for
-- each of six pulses (07/23 400, 10/24 100, 12/24 2%, 04/25 1.5%, 04/26
-- 1.5%, 04/27 1%), A — the shekel supplements the retiree had as an active
-- employee before retiring — and B — the percentage supplements (in ח4',
-- the rate his basic salary had been raised from the authority's salary
-- base). A cell is blank where the pulse does not reach the month (¶1, the
-- corpus's own note: the printed table shades them); the last row names
-- the last pulse, 4.2027, and holds nothing.
@desc A row of annex ח2' or ח4': the month of retiring, X, and each pulse's A and B (NOTHING where blank).
DECLARE `2023 retiree row` HAS
    `the month he retired in` IS A NUMBER
    `the year he retired in` IS A NUMBER
    `X of the row` IS A NUMBER
    `A at each pulse` IS A LIST OF MAYBE NUMBER
    `B at each pulse` IS A LIST OF MAYBE NUMBER

`the pulses of annexes ח2'–ח4'` MEANS
    LIST `the 2023 framework's month` 2023 7, `the 2023 framework's month` 2024 10, `the 2023 framework's month` 2024 12,
         `the 2023 framework's month` 2025 4, `the 2023 framework's month` 2026 4, `the 2023 framework's month` 2027 4

-- X is the months of the 2020–2027 frame he served, from January 2020 to
-- the month he retired, over 96, to a hundredth of a percent.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `X for one who retired in` m y IS
    ((`the 2023 framework's month` y m MINUS `the 2023 framework's month` 2019 12) DIVIDED BY 96) `to the nearest` 0.0001

-- What §90(ב) asks of a pulse: a pulse after the month he retired reaches
-- him, with A and B as he had them when he retired; a pulse in or before
-- it does not (he had it as an active employee).
GIVEN r IS A `2023 retiree row`, p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the A §90(ב) asks at` r p IS
    IF p GREATER THAN `the 2023 framework's month` (r's `the year he retired in`) (r's `the month he retired in`)
    THEN JUST (`the 2023 shekel supplement for a full position on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (r's `the month he retired in`) (r's `the year he retired in`)) FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN r IS A `2023 retiree row`, p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the B §90(ב) asks at` r p IS
    IF p GREATER THAN `the 2023 framework's month` (r's `the year he retired in`) (r's `the month he retired in`)
    THEN JUST (`the 2024 percentage supplement rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (r's `the month he retired in`) (r's `the year he retired in`)) TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The cells of a table where its A does not follow §90(ב): (month, year,
-- pulse number from 1).
DECLARE `2023 retiree cell` HAS
    `the cell's month` IS A NUMBER
    `the cell's year` IS A NUMBER
    `the cell's pulse` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN rows IS A LIST OF `2023 retiree row`
GIVETH A LIST OF `2023 retiree cell`
DECIDE `the A cells that do not follow §90(ב) in` rows IS
    concat (map (GIVEN r YIELD
                     map (GIVEN t YIELD `2023 retiree cell` (r's `the month he retired in`) (r's `the year he retired in`) (snd t))
                         (filter (GIVEN t YIELD NOT ((fst t) EQUALS `the A §90(ב) asks at` r (at `the pulses of annexes ח2'–ח4'` ((snd t) MINUS 1))))
                                 (zip (r's `A at each pulse`) (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6))))
                rows)

GIVEN rows IS A LIST OF `2023 retiree row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `every B and X of the table follows §90` rows IF
    all (GIVEN r YIELD
                 r's `X of the row` EQUALS `X for one who retired in` (r's `the month he retired in`) (r's `the year he retired in`)
             AND all (GIVEN t YIELD (fst t) EQUALS `the B §90(ב) asks at` r (at `the pulses of annexes ח2'–ח4'` ((snd t) MINUS 1)))
                     (zip (r's `B at each pulse`) (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6)))
        rows

@ref akn:att_9__hc_1/p1 akn:att_9__hc_1/t1 akn:att_11__hc_1/p1 akn:att_11__hc_1/t1
#ASSERT count `the rows of annex ח2'` EQUALS 87
#ASSERT `every B and X of the table follows §90` `the rows of annex ח2'`
#ASSERT `every B and X of the table follows §90` `the rows of annex ח4'`
#ASSERT `the rows of annex ח4'` EQUALS `the rows of annex ח2'`

-- F-framework-2023-e: the A of nine cells does not follow §90(ב)'s
-- definition — "the 2023 shekel supplement the eligible retiree had on the
-- eve of retiring". One who retired in 6.2023 (before the 400 of 1.7.2023)
-- has A = 0 at pulse 1 and A = 400 at pulses 2–6, in the same row; one who
-- retired in 9.2024 (with 400, before the 100 of 1.10.2024) has A = 400 at
-- pulse 2 and A = 500 at pulses 3–6. ח4' prints the same. The printed
-- table governs (convention precedence.table): A at each pulse is the
-- cell's.
`the A cells annexes ח2' and ח4' print against §90(ב)` MEANS
    LIST `2023 retiree cell` 6 2023 2, `2023 retiree cell` 6 2023 3, `2023 retiree cell` 6 2023 4, `2023 retiree cell` 6 2023 5, `2023 retiree cell` 6 2023 6,
         `2023 retiree cell` 9 2024 3, `2023 retiree cell` 9 2024 4, `2023 retiree cell` 9 2024 5, `2023 retiree cell` 9 2024 6

`annexes ח2' and ח4' print an A the retiree did not have on the eve` MEANS
        `the A cells that do not follow §90(ב) in` `the rows of annex ח2'` EQUALS `the A cells annexes ח2' and ח4' print against §90(ב)`
    AND `the A cells that do not follow §90(ב) in` `the rows of annex ח4'` EQUALS `the A cells annexes ח2' and ח4' print against §90(ב)`

#ASSERT `annexes ח2' and ח4' print an A the retiree did not have on the eve`

GIVEN rows IS A LIST OF `2023 retiree row`
      m IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
      pulse IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the A the 2023 table prints for` rows m y pulse IS
    foldl (GIVEN acc, r YIELD
               IF r's `the month he retired in` EQUALS m AND r's `the year he retired in` EQUALS y
               THEN at (r's `A at each pulse`) (pulse MINUS 1)
               ELSE acc)
          NOTHING rows

#ASSERT `the A the 2023 table prints for` `the rows of annex ח2'` 6 2023 1 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `the A the 2023 table prints for` `the rows of annex ח2'` 6 2023 2 EQUALS JUST 400

-- One who retired in 6.2023 (X = 43.75%) with a C of 10,000: at the third
-- pulse the table's A of 400 leaves Y = 0 and M = 181.25, so S = 37.5;
-- §90(ב)'s A of 0 would give S = 437.5.
#ASSERT `S of the 2023 pensioners on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2024) (43.75%) 400 0 10000 EQUALS 37.5
#ASSERT `S of the 2023 pensioners on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2024) (43.75%) 0 0 10000 EQUALS 437.5

-- ח3', the border crossings: for each grade, G and A over the periods (to
-- 30.6.2023 "-", read as nothing raised; 7/23–9/24; 10/24–11/24;
-- 12/24–3/25; 4/25–3/26; 4/26–3/27; from 4/27); and the coefficients X by
-- the month of retiring. G is the last period's A; each A is the border
-- table's rise over its first column, to the agora; X is ח2''s.
@ref akn:att_10__hc_1/t1 akn:att_10__hc_1/t2 akn:att_10__hc_1/t3 akn:att_10__hc_1/t4 akn:att_10__hc_1/t5 akn:att_10__hc_1/t6 akn:att_10__hc_1/t7
DECLARE `2023 coefficient` HAS
    `the coefficient's month` IS A NUMBER
    `the coefficient's year` IS A NUMBER
    `the coefficient` IS A NUMBER

#ASSERT map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the coefficient`) `the coefficients X of annex ח3'` EQUALS map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `X of the row`) `the rows of annex ח2'`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the coefficient` EQUALS `X for one who retired in` (c's `the coefficient's month`) (c's `the coefficient's year`)) `the coefficients X of annex ח3'`

GIVEN g IS A `2023 annex row`, b IS A `2023 annex row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a ח3' row is the border table's rises` g b IF
    CONSIDER g's `the 2023 row's cells`
    WHEN `the G` FOLLOWED BY `the As` THEN
        (CONSIDER b's `the 2023 row's cells`
         WHEN b0 FOLLOWED BY brest THEN
                 count `the As` EQUALS count (b's `the 2023 row's cells`)
             AND all (GIVEN p YIELD (fst p) `is within an agora of` ((snd p) MINUS b0)) (zip `the As` (b's `the 2023 row's cells`))
             AND `the G` `is within an agora of` (at (b's `the 2023 row's cells`) 6 MINUS b0)
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

#ASSERT all (GIVEN p YIELD `a ח3' row is the border table's rises` (fst p) (snd p)) (zip `the G and A of annex ח3'` `the border crossings' basic table of 2023`)

